#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""evolve — the code half of Evolve, the self-improvement loop (docs/self-improvement-2026-10-30.md). Stdlib, 3.9.

    evolve probes [--doc FILE]... [--board [--limit N]] [--json] [--no-record]
        The owner's answer surface, probed end to end at zero tokens: exit 0 when every stage holds,
        1 naming each that does not, 2 when a tool it drives is missing.
    evolve coverage [--scope S [--open | --promote] [--session ID]] [--since TIME] [--json] [--no-record]
        The register — lens x source x scope — from lenses.json and each scope's profile, the surface
        nothing reads, and each scope's collector manifest: exit 0 when every cell is seen and the surface
        is read, 1 naming each blind spot, 2 when the registry or lenses.json cannot be read.
    evolve conformance [--scope S] [--days 7] [--json] [--no-record]
        The declared rules against the transcripts' tool calls: exit 0 when every rule holds, 1 when one is
        dead, violated or worked around (or none is declared), 2 when the registry or a rule cannot be read.
    evolve validate KIND FILE [--scope S] [--quiet] · evolve schema [KIND] · evolve action-id FINDING_ID VERSION SCOPE
        A record (a .jsonl file: each line) against its schema (lib/evolve_schema.py); the schemas; an
        action's identity.
    evolve where SCOPE [--day D] · evolve open SCOPE [--day D] [--session ID] [--quiet-exit] [--json]
        Where the scope pass reads and writes (`atlas` records in the vault, staged outside it); the pass's
        zero-token collectors, carried findings, tonight's research check, rotating deep lens and opening
        manifest (exit 3 under --quiet-exit when quiet is earned at zero tokens).
    evolve critic FILE [--scope S] [--json] · evolve record SCOPE [--day D] [--quiet] [--session ID] [--cost USD]
        The blinded critic over a cold findings artefact (gate `evolve.critic`); the pass's record gate.
    evolve meetings [PATH | --scope S] [--json] · evolve replay --cutoff D [...] · evolve shadow --scope S [...]
        Repo-committed meeting pre-briefs and if-then commitments; hidden-future replay; shadow scope pass.

**Why it exists** (Evolve S2; the scope-pass component's lens 3). The owner's asks about the live
surfaces — a course link that opens nothing, an answer nobody picked up, a board card that never came —
came to about 45 in 60 days (the answer surface in 17 sessions, links that open where the owner is in
10) and nothing probed them: the dream saw only the complaint, after it. A probe walks the journey a
decision takes, each stage through the verb the live system uses, and says which stage broke before the
owner meets it:

  board     keel list (helm's board reads it) lists the doc with its decisions open
  link      every local file link in the doc opens on this Mac (the path, or the same path under this
            Mac's projects root when another Mac's home wrote it), and has a GitHub address
  render    keel build --form: a field per decision, and every link that has an address is a link on
            the page — not `[x](/path)` as text, which is what every course page showed until keel's
            local_href (2026-10-31)
  saved     keel merge --write: the form's store document (an answer per item) is written into the doc
  ingested  keel parse reads every decision answered
  resumed   keel status --stamp moves the doc's Status line to answered, and keel list stops counting
            its decisions open: the step that waited on them may run

The journey runs on a synthetic doc in a scratch repo (a GitHub-shaped origin, its refs set locally: no
network, nothing live is written). `--doc FILE` (repeatable) and `--board` (the docs `keel list` finds
with decisions open, newest first, `--limit` of them, default 10) add the read-only stages, link and
render, on real docs: the render goes to a scratch file. A doc of a confidential scope (the core's
gather_fence: an unreadable registry fences every doc) is neither read nor named: the run counts it
(`fenced`), since its record is global. The link stage reads links with keel's own rule (its
LOCAL_LINK_RE over the text as inline() escapes it, and its local_candidates), so the probe judges what
the page renders. A run appends one line to
`<log dir>/aurora/evolve/probes.jsonl` (the core's LOG_DIR; EVOLVE_STATE replaces the folder) — the
stage verdicts and counts, never a doc's text — for the coverage lens (S3) and G2, the asks after a
shipped mechanism; `--no-record` skips it.

**coverage** (Evolve S3; the scope-pass component's "By construction"). A blind spot is what nothing reads,
found by construction, never by a model guessing. For every scope of the registry (read once through the
core's read_registry(): a torn one fails closed, exit 2; every scope walked, never the first that lists a
repo) and every source of every lens, a cell: `not_applicable` (the profile says so), `excluded` (a reason
and a review date; past it, overdue), `fenced` (a path of another confidential scope's: never judged),
`inaccessible` (declared, and not readable on this yard: the repo is not on this host, or the file cannot
be read), `source_missing` (the root is here, nothing at the path; a verb not installed), `unread` (nothing
reads it into a lens: its reader is null or not installed, or it is `pass` and the pass's section —
evolve-scope.md once S5 writes it, dream-scope.md until then — names neither its id, its verb nor its file),
`stale` (older than the source's `fresh_days` by its newest record's own time — the value, not the
timestamp: the freshest member for `need: any`, the oldest for `all`), else `observed`. A member repo or a
path of another confidential scope (an open scope's glob may list one) is skipped, never judged. The surface diff lists every
registry repo in no scope and each entry of the log dir and the config dir no source reads (never through
a link: the config dir links synced cloud folders). The **collector manifest** (`<state>/manifests/<scope>.json`)
is what a `quiet` receipt (S5) rests on, judged against the last COMPLETE pass's manifest
(`<scope>.complete.json`, which only `--promote` writes, copying the manifest the pass's opening run wrote:
the pass runs `coverage --scope S --open --session ID` as it starts and `--promote` once its receipt is
complete, so a run that only looked consumes no change, what landed while the pass ran is still one, and
the pass's own output — `dreams/`, `evolve/`, its records branch, its session — is none): every required collector's sources seen fresh — a verb's only with
its run receipt, `<state>/receipts/<scope>/<cell's source id>.json` {"time"} (a confidential
scope's profile source by its neutral id), which the pass writes when it ran it —
no change in lenses.json, the profile, the North Star or the scope's registry entry, no commit in its repos
outside the pass's output, no session of the scope newer than the baseline, no record (judged by when it was
written; a record stamped ahead of the clock is read as now) newer than
the baseline's cutoff (`--since` overrides) in a source that wakes the scope (its own repos' always, a
shared log's only where lenses.json marks it `wakes`: the ops desk writes every quarter hour), no exclusion
past its review; else `quiet_ok` false with why. A
confidential scope is judged only under its own --scope (its pass, inside): a global run counts it
(`skipped_confidential`) and opens nothing of it, since what leaves one is its checked lines and its receipt
word. It is named by the core's scope_marker() in every output and record, its profile's own
source ids and reasons never shown; its manifest files, which stay on the host, keep its hashes and its heads
under hashed keys, never a repo's path. The surface lists no worktree apart: every member's worktree
branches are among the heads the manifest reads, and a repo in no scope is listed as its repo. One line a run in `<state>/coverage.jsonl`: ids, states and counts.

**conformance** (lens 11: work-as-imagined against work-as-done). Rules live in the overlay
(`<config>/aurora/conformance.json`) and a scope's profile (`conformance`, read on that scope's transcripts
only; a confidential scope's only under its own --scope, where its transcripts are read): {id, ref, tool, when, breach}, regexes over a tool call's command (Bash) or its input. Over the
window's tool calls in every login dir's transcripts, the subagents' included — a confidential scope's
judged on its path and never opened (the S1 trap) — a rule is `dead` (never applied), `holds` (applied,
never breached, or every breach refused by a guard: an error result in a PreToolUse hook's or the
permission system's own shape; a call with no result, or one the classifier gave no verdict on, is
`unknown`, neither ok nor failed, and a rule whose breaches are all unknown is `unknown`, never holds; one call
counted once, by its id, however many files carry it, with the outcome a copy knows), `worked_around` (breaches that succeeded `workaround_min` times in `workaround_sessions`
sessions: a candidate for promotion, not punishment) or `violated`. One line a run in
`<state>/conformance.jsonl`: rule ids and counts, never a command's text.

Not probed, and said in every run: whether the spacesheep page deploys (`keel line` deploys a live
page), whether VS Code opens a link (no script can click it), and the owner's phone.
"""
import argparse
import datetime as dt
import fnmatch
import functools
import glob as globmod
import hashlib
import html
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time
from pathlib import Path

HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
sys.path.insert(0, str(HERE.parent / "lib"))
import find_core  # noqa: E402  the regatta core's hooks/; none: one line, exit 2
sys.path.insert(0, find_core.hooks())
import common  # noqa: E402  tool, LOG_DIR, PROJECTS
import evolve_schema as schema  # noqa: E402  the finding, coverage, receipt and ledger schemas (S3)

PROG = "evolve"
STAGES = ("board", "link", "render", "saved", "ingested", "resumed")
NOT_PROBED = "not probed: the spacesheep deploy (keel line deploys a live page), VS Code opening a link, the phone"
CODE_SPAN = re.compile(r"`[^`\n]*`")
# the same link as a rendered page would show it, escaped: what keel left as text before local_href
RAW_ON_PAGE = re.compile(r"\[[^\]<>\n]+\]\((?:/|~/|&lt;)")


def keel_bin():
    """keel in this checkout's modules (a branch probes its own keel), else the core's peer lookup.
    EVOLVE_KEEL replaces it (a suite's stand-in)."""
    if os.environ.get("EVOLVE_KEEL"):
        return Path(os.environ["EVOLVE_KEEL"])
    here = HERE.parent.parent / "keel" / "bin" / "keel"
    if here.is_file():
        return here
    k = common.tool("keel")
    return Path(k) if k else None


_KEEL = None


def keel_mod():
    """keel, loaded as a module (its local_href is the one rule for where a link goes)."""
    global _KEEL
    if _KEEL is None:
        from importlib.machinery import SourceFileLoader
        argv, sys.argv = sys.argv, ["keel"]
        try:
            _KEEL = SourceFileLoader("keel_for_evolve", str(keel_bin())).load_module()
        finally:
            sys.argv = argv
    return _KEEL


def keel(*args, cwd=None, timeout=120):
    try:
        return subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(keel_bin()), *map(str, args)], capture_output=True, text=True,
                              cwd=cwd, timeout=timeout, env={**os.environ, "GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT": "0"})
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        return subprocess.CompletedProcess(args, 124, "", "timed out after %ss" % timeout)


def git(repo, *a):
    return subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(repo), *a], capture_output=True, text=True,
                          env={**os.environ, "GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT": "0"})


def local_links(text):
    """[(label, target)] — the doc's local file links outside code spans and fences, read as keel's
    inline() reads them: its LOCAL_LINK_RE over the escaped line (S2 landing review, finding 16)."""
    rx = getattr(keel_mod(), "LOCAL_LINK_RE", None) or re.compile(r"\[([^\]\n]+)\]\((&lt;[^\n]+?&gt;|(?:/|~/)[^)\s]*)\)")
    out, fence = [], False
    for line in text.split("\n"):
        if line.lstrip().startswith(("```", "~~~")):
            fence = not fence
            continue
        if fence:
            continue
        for m in rx.finditer(html.escape(CODE_SPAN.sub("", line), quote=False)):
            t = html.unescape(m.group(2))
            out.append((html.unescape(m.group(1)), t[1:-1] if t.startswith("<") else t))
    return out


def opens_here(target):
    """Does the link's file exist on this Mac, by keel's candidate rule (local_candidates: as written, or
    under this Mac's projects root)?"""
    path = target.partition("#")[0]
    cands = getattr(keel_mod(), "local_candidates", None)
    return any(c.exists() for c in (cands(path) if cands else [Path(path).expanduser()]))


def stage(name, ok, detail):
    return {"stage": name, "ok": bool(ok), "detail": detail}


def probe_link(doc, text):
    links = local_links(text)
    dead = [t for _, t in links if not opens_here(t)]
    href = getattr(keel_mod(), "local_href", None)
    if href is None:   # a keel before 2026-10-31: no address for any local link
        return stage("link", False, "%d local link%s; this keel has no local_href, so none has a GitHub address" % (
            len(links), "" if len(links) == 1 else "s")), links
    nowhere = [t for _, t in links if t not in dead and not href(t)]
    ok = not dead and not nowhere
    detail = "%d local link%s: %d open here, %d with a GitHub address" % (
        len(links), "" if len(links) == 1 else "s", len(links) - len(dead), len(links) - len(dead) - len(nowhere))
    if dead:
        detail += "; open nothing here: " + ", ".join(Path(t.partition("#")[0]).name for t in dead[:5])
    if nowhere:
        detail += "; no GitHub address (on no origin ref): " + ", ".join(Path(t.partition("#")[0]).name for t in nowhere[:5])
    return stage("link", ok, detail), links


def probe_render(doc, text, links, scratch):
    out = Path(scratch) / ("%s.html" % Path(doc).stem)
    r = keel("build", doc, "-o", out)
    if r.returncode != 0 or not out.is_file():
        return stage("render", False, "keel build failed: %s" % ((r.stderr or r.stdout).strip().splitlines() or ["no output"])[-1][:200])
    page = out.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
    p = keel("parse", doc)
    try:
        ids = [i["id"] for i in json.loads(p.stdout)["items"]]
    except (ValueError, KeyError):
        return stage("render", False, "keel parse failed on the doc")
    missing = [i for i in ids if 'id="ans-%s"' % i not in page]
    # the symptom itself: a local link left as markdown text on the page (outside a code span)
    visible = re.sub(r"<(script|style|code)\b.*?</\1>", "", page, flags=re.S | re.I)
    shown = len(RAW_ON_PAGE.findall(re.sub(r"<[^>]*>", "", visible)))   # text, never an attribute (data-q)
    ok = not missing and not shown
    detail = "%d field%s for %d decision%s; %d local link%s, %d shown as text, not a link" % (
        len(ids) - len(missing), "" if len(ids) - len(missing) == 1 else "s", len(ids), "" if len(ids) == 1 else "s",
        len(links), "" if len(links) == 1 else "s", shown)
    if missing:
        detail += "; no field for " + ", ".join(missing)
    return stage("render", ok, detail)


FIXTURE = """# Probe — the owner's answer surface ({day})

Status: proposed — 0 of 2 decisions answered · handed over {day}

**Legend.** D<n> a decision only the owner makes. Written by `evolve probes` in a scratch repo; nothing
here is live.

What the decisions rest on: [the target]({target}#L1).

## Decisions

- **D1 — The first probe decision**
  - A — the first option
  - B — the second option

  Reversible: yes

  ➤ Recommended: A

  ➤ Answer:

- **D2 — The second probe decision**
  - A — the first option
  - B — the second option

  Reversible: yes

  ➤ Recommended: B

  ➤ Answer:

## Open feedback
"""


def journey(scratch):
    """The six stages on a synthetic doc in a scratch repo. [stage dict]."""
    day = dt.date.today().isoformat()
    root = Path(scratch) / "projects"
    repo = root / "probe-demo"
    (repo / "docs").mkdir(parents=True)
    env_id = ["-c", "user.name=evolve probes", "-c", "user.email=probes@example.invalid"]
    target = repo / "docs" / "target.md"
    target.write_text("# The target\n\nA file a decision rests on.\n", encoding="utf-8")
    doc = repo / "docs" / ("probe-%s.md" % day)
    doc.write_text(FIXTURE.format(day=day, target=target), encoding="utf-8")
    steps = [git(repo, "init", "-q", "-b", "main"), git(repo, "add", "-A"),
             git(repo, *env_id, "commit", "-q", "-m", "probe fixture"),
             git(repo, "remote", "add", "origin", "https://github.com/probe/probe-demo.git"),
             git(repo, "update-ref", "refs/remotes/origin/main", "HEAD")]
    bad = next((s for s in steps if s.returncode != 0), None)
    if bad:
        return [stage("board", False, "the scratch repo could not be made: %s" % (bad.stderr or bad.stdout).strip()[:200])]
    out = []
    text = doc.read_text(encoding="utf-8")

    def listed():
        r = keel("list", "--root", root, "--json", "--limit", "50")
        try:
            return next((row for row in json.loads(r.stdout) if Path(row.get("path", "")).resolve() == doc.resolve()), None)
        except ValueError:
            return None
    row = listed()
    out.append(stage("board", row is not None and row.get("open") == 2,
                     "keel list: %s" % ("the doc with %s of %s decisions open" % (row.get("open"), row.get("decisions")) if row
                                        else "the doc is not listed — helm's board would show no card")))
    s, links = probe_link(doc, text)
    out.append(s)
    out.append(probe_render(doc, text, links, scratch))
    answers = Path(scratch) / "answers.json"
    answers.write_text(json.dumps({"data": {"items": {"D1": "A", "D2": "B — the second option"}, "feedback": "",
                                            "savedAt": dt.datetime.now().astimezone().isoformat(timespec="seconds"),
                                            "version": 1}}), encoding="utf-8")
    m = keel("merge", doc, answers, "--write")
    after = doc.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    out.append(stage("saved", m.returncode == 0 and after != text and "changed: D1, D2" in (m.stdout + m.stderr),
                     "keel merge --write: %s" % (((m.stdout or m.stderr).strip().splitlines() or ["no output"])[-1][:160])))
    p = keel("parse", doc)
    try:
        d = json.loads(p.stdout)
        answered = sum(1 for i in d["items"] if (i.get("answer") or "").strip())
        dec = d.get("keel", {}).get("decisions")
    except (ValueError, KeyError):
        answered, dec = 0, None
    out.append(stage("ingested", answered == 2 and dec == [2, 2],
                     "keel parse: %d of 2 answered, decisions %s" % (answered, dec)))
    st = keel("status", "--stamp", doc)
    line = next((l for l in doc.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines() if l.startswith("Status:")), "")
    row = listed()
    out.append(stage("resumed", line.startswith("Status: answered") and row is not None and row.get("open") == 0,
                     "keel status --stamp: %s; keel list: %s open" % (
                         (line[:70] or "no Status line") if st.returncode == 0 else "exit %d" % st.returncode,
                         row.get("open") if row else "not listed")))
    return out


def board_docs(limit):
    r = keel("list", "--root", common.PROJECTS, "--json", "--limit", "200", timeout=300)
    try:
        rows = json.loads(r.stdout)
    except ValueError:
        return []
    return [Path(row["path"]) for row in rows if (row.get("open") or 0) > 0][:limit]


def record(result):
    return append_record("probes.jsonl", result)   # one state dir, one writer (S3's review: no second copy)


def cmd_probes(a):
    if not keel_bin() or not keel_bin().is_file():
        print("%s probes: keel is not installed — nothing to probe the answer surface with" % PROG, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    result = {"time": dt.datetime.now().astimezone().isoformat(timespec="seconds"), "journey": [], "docs": [],
              "not_probed": NOT_PROBED}
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="evolve-probes-") as scratch:
        result["journey"] = journey(scratch)
        docs = [Path(p).expanduser() for p in a.doc] + (board_docs(a.limit) if a.board else [])
        # a confidential scope's doc is neither read nor named here: the record is global (finding 10)
        try:
            fence = common.gather_fence()
        except ValueError:
            fence = lambda *paths: "fenced"   # noqa: E731  a registry no reader can trust fences everything
        kept = [p for p in docs if fence(str(p), str(p.resolve()) if p.exists() else str(p)) == "quote"]
        result["fenced"] = len(docs) - len(kept)
        for p in kept:
            if not p.is_file():
                result["docs"].append({"doc": p.name, "stages": [stage("link", False, "no such file")]})
                continue
            text = p.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
            s, links = probe_link(p, text)
            result["docs"].append({"doc": p.name, "stages": [s, probe_render(p, text, links, scratch)]})
    fails = [s for s in result["journey"] if not s["ok"]] + [s for d in result["docs"] for s in d["stages"] if not s["ok"]]
    result["ok"] = not fails
    if not a.no_record:
        record({**result, "docs": [{"doc": d["doc"], "stages": [{"stage": s["stage"], "ok": s["ok"]} for s in d["stages"]]}
                                   for d in result["docs"]]})
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps(result, indent=1))
    else:
        print("journey (a synthetic doc in a scratch repo):")
        for s in result["journey"]:
            print("  %s %-8s %s" % ("ok  " if s["ok"] else "FAIL", s["stage"], s["detail"]))
        for d in result["docs"]:
            print("%s:" % d["doc"])
            for s in d["stages"]:
                print("  %s %-8s %s" % ("ok  " if s["ok"] else "FAIL", s["stage"], s["detail"]))
        if result["fenced"]:
            print("%d doc%s of a confidential scope: fenced, not probed or named here" % (
                result["fenced"], "" if result["fenced"] == 1 else "s"))
        print(NOT_PROBED)
        print("probes: %s" % ("every stage holds" if not fails else "%d stage%s broken" % (len(fails), "" if len(fails) == 1 else "s")))
    return 0 if not fails else 1


# ---- S3: the register, the surface diff, the collector manifest, conformance, the schemas ------------------

LENSES = HERE.parent / "lenses.json"
SECTIONS = HERE.parent / "skills" / "aurora" / "sections"
RANK = {"observed": 0, "stale": 1, "source_missing": 2, "inaccessible": 3}
NOT_SEEN = ("stale", "source_missing", "unread", "inaccessible")
TIME_KEYS = ("time", "ts", "at", "as_of", "created", "timestamp", "date", "ended", "started")   # as_of: ops' rows; created: its intake;
# ended, started: build-review's (the finish review)
ROOTS = ("{log}", "{config}", "{anchor}", "{repo}")
OWN_ROOTS = ("{anchor}", "{repo}")   # the scope's own: a record there wakes it; a shared log's only when marked
# what a confidential scope's profile source says in place of its own words (finding 1, S3's first review)
NEUTRAL = {"source_missing": "nothing there", "inaccessible": "not readable on this host", "unread": "nothing reads it yet",
           "stale": "older than its freshness", "fenced": "another confidential scope's", "excluded": "excluded by the profile",
           "not_applicable": "the profile says so"}
VERB_RECEIPT_DAYS = 7


def valid_day(v):
    """V when it is a real YYYY-MM-DD date, else None: a review date that does not read lapses at once."""
    return v if isinstance(v, str) and re.fullmatch(schema.DAY, v) and schema._is_date(v) else None


class Refused(Exception):
    """A refusal the verb names and exits 2 on (never 1, which means blind spots: AGENTS.md's probe trap)."""


def state_dir():
    return Path(os.environ.get("EVOLVE_STATE") or Path(common.LOG_DIR) / "aurora" / "evolve")


def lenses_path():
    return Path(os.environ.get("EVOLVE_LENSES") or LENSES)


def sections_dir():
    return Path(os.environ.get("EVOLVE_SECTIONS") or SECTIONS)


def source_problem(s, where):
    """None, or why a source declaration cannot be judged: an id, a known kind, a path under a root (a bare
    or relative path would be judged against the cwd), a verb by name, a number of days."""
    if not isinstance(s, dict) or not isinstance(s.get("id"), str) or not s["id"]:
        return "%s: a source with no id" % where
    k = s.get("kind")
    if k not in ("path", "verb", "git"):
        return "%s: source %s: unknown kind %r" % (where, s["id"], k)
    if k == "path" and not (isinstance(s.get("at"), str) and s["at"].startswith(ROOTS)):
        return "%s: source %s: its `at` starts with none of %s" % (where, s["id"], ", ".join(ROOTS))
    if k == "verb" and not (isinstance(s.get("name"), str) and s["name"] and "/" not in s["name"]):
        return "%s: source %s: a verb needs a tool's name" % (where, s["id"])
    if s.get("need") is not None and s.get("need") not in ("any", "all"):
        return "%s: source %s: need is any or all, not %r" % (where, s["id"], s.get("need"))
    fd = s.get("fresh_days")
    if fd is not None and (isinstance(fd, bool) or not isinstance(fd, (int, float))):
        return "%s: source %s: fresh_days is no number" % (where, s["id"])
    if s.get("reader") is not None and not isinstance(s.get("reader"), str):
        return "%s: source %s: reader is no name" % (where, s["id"])
    return None


def load_lenses():
    """lenses.json, read with open() (classes.sh never sees it: it is named on autofinish_exclude by hand),
    and checked: unique lens and source ids, every source judgeable, every collector naming a declared source."""
    p = lenses_path()
    with open(p, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        raw = fh.read()
    d = json.loads(raw)
    lenses = d.get("lenses") if isinstance(d, dict) else None
    if not isinstance(lenses, list) or not lenses:
        raise ValueError("no lenses")
    seen, ids = set(), set()
    for ln in lenses:
        if not isinstance(ln, dict) or not isinstance(ln.get("id"), str) or ln["id"] in ids:
            raise ValueError("a lens with no id, or one id twice")
        ids.add(ln["id"])
        for s in ln.get("sources") or []:
            why = source_problem(s, "lens %s" % ln["id"])
            if why:
                raise ValueError(why)
            if s["id"] in seen:
                raise ValueError("source %s declared twice" % s["id"])
            seen.add(s["id"])
    cols = d.get("collectors") or []
    if not isinstance(cols, list) or any(not isinstance(c, dict) for c in cols):
        raise ValueError("collectors is no list of objects")
    for c in cols:
        missing = [s for s in c.get("sources") or [] if s not in seen]
        if missing:
            raise ValueError("collector %r names no declared source %s" % (c.get("id"), missing))
    d["_sha"], d["_lens_ids"], d["_source_ids"] = hashlib.sha256(raw.encode("utf-8")).hexdigest(), ids, seen
    return d


def file_sha(p):
    """The hash of a JSON file's content, parsed and dumped sorted, so a reindent or a key reorder is no change
    (engineering.md: compare structured files structurally; the finish review); its bytes where it is no JSON."""
    try:
        with open(p, "rb") as fh:
            raw = fh.read()
    except OSError:
        return None
    try:
        raw = json.dumps(json.loads(raw), sort_keys=True, separators=(",", ":")).encode("utf-8")
    except ValueError:
        pass
    return hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()


def parse_time(v):
    if isinstance(v, (int, float)) and not isinstance(v, bool):   # an epoch, in seconds or milliseconds
        try:
            return dt.datetime.fromtimestamp(v if v < 1e11 else v / 1000).astimezone()
        except (OverflowError, OSError, ValueError):
            return None
    t = schema.read_time(v, date_ok=True)
    return None if t is None else t if t.tzinfo else t.astimezone()


def newest_value(p):
    """The newest time a file's records carry — the value, not the timestamp (engineering rules): a JSON
    lines file's last parseable line's time, a JSON object's own; the file's mtime otherwise."""
    try:
        if p.suffix in (".jsonl", ".json"):
            with open(p, "rb") as fh:
                fh.seek(0, 2)
                fh.seek(max(0, fh.tell() - 65536))
                tail = fh.read().decode("utf-8", "replace")
            for line in reversed(tail.strip().splitlines() if p.suffix == ".jsonl" else [tail]):
                try:
                    rec = json.loads(line)
                except ValueError:
                    continue
                for k in TIME_KEYS if isinstance(rec, dict) else ():
                    t = parse_time(rec.get(k)) if rec.get(k) not in (None, "") else None
                    if t:
                        return t
                break
        return dt.datetime.fromtimestamp(p.stat().st_mtime).astimezone()
    except OSError:
        return None


def judge_path(p, root_here):
    """(state, newest, why, written) for one declared path: `inaccessible` when its root (the scope's anchor or a
    member repo) is not on this host or the path cannot be read here, `source_missing` when the root is
    here and nothing is at the path; else observed with its newest time (staleness is judged later). A
    linked folder is judged by its own time, never listed: a link may lead into a synced drive."""
    if not root_here:
        return "inaccessible", None, "declared, and its repo is not on this host", None
    try:
        st = p.stat()
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return "source_missing", None, "nothing at the declared path", None
    except OSError:
        return "inaccessible", None, "declared, and unreadable here", None
    if p.is_dir():
        if not os.access(p, os.R_OK | os.X_OK):
            return "inaccessible", None, "declared, and unreadable here", None
        times = [st.st_mtime]
        if not p.is_symlink():
            try:
                times += [c.lstat().st_mtime for c in p.iterdir()]
            except OSError:
                return "inaccessible", None, "declared, and unreadable here", None
        t = dt.datetime.fromtimestamp(max(times)).astimezone()
        return "observed", t, None, t
    if not os.access(p, os.R_OK):
        return "inaccessible", None, "declared, and unreadable here", None
    # the record's own time judges staleness; a change is whichever is later, it or the write (a record stamped
    # before the cutoff and written after it is still new: round 3)
    return "observed", newest_value(p), None, dt.datetime.fromtimestamp(st.st_mtime).astimezone()


@functools.lru_cache(maxsize=None)
def peer(name):
    """A peer tool: this checkout's modules first (a branch judges its own), then the core's lookup."""
    if not name or "/" in name or name in (".", ".."):
        return None
    hits = sorted(p for p in HERE.parent.parent.glob("*/bin/%s" % globmod.escape(name)) if p.is_file())
    return hits[0] if hits else common.tool(name)


_SECTION = {}


def section_text():
    """(name, text) of the scope pass's section: evolve-scope.md (S5) once it exists, else dream-scope.md."""
    if "t" not in _SECTION:
        d = sections_dir()
        f = d / "evolve-scope.md" if (d / "evolve-scope.md").is_file() else d / "dream-scope.md"
        try:
            _SECTION["t"] = (f.name, f.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except OSError:
            _SECTION["t"] = (None, "")
    return _SECTION["t"]


FENCE_BLOCK = re.compile(r"^[ \t]*(```|~~~)[^\n]*\n(.*?)^[ \t]*\1", re.M | re.S)


def code_text(text):
    """What the section runs or names as code: the bodies of its fenced blocks and each inline code span,
    paired properly (a pattern that spans from one span's closing backtick to the next's opening one reads
    prose as code: round 4)."""
    blocks = [m.group(2) for m in FENCE_BLOCK.finditer(text)]
    rest = FENCE_BLOCK.sub("", text)
    return "\n".join(blocks + CODE_SPAN.findall(rest))


def anchor_text(scope, fenced_by):
    """The anchor's own `.claude/scope-pass.md`, once a run — never another confidential scope's (an open
    scope whose first repo is one: round 4)."""
    if not hasattr(scope, "_anchor_text"):
        scope._anchor_text = None
        if scope.anchor is not None and not (fenced_by and fenced_by(scope.anchor)):
            try:
                scope._anchor_text = (scope.anchor / ".claude" / "scope-pass.md").read_text(encoding="utf-8")
            except OSError:
                pass
    return scope._anchor_text


def reader_here(src, scope=None, fenced_by=None):
    """(read, why). `pass` reads a source only where the pass's section (or the anchor's own
    `.claude/scope-pass.md`, where a confidential scope names what the public section cannot) names it — its
    id or its verb as code (a fenced block or an inline span), or its file's name — so prose never makes a
    source read (rounds 1, 3, 4)."""
    reader = src.get("reader")
    if reader is None:
        return False, "nothing reads it yet"
    if reader == "pass":
        name, text = section_text()
        own = anchor_text(scope, fenced_by) if scope is not None else None   # the scope's own judgement, never public
        if own is not None:
            text, name = text + "\n" + own, name or "scope-pass.md"
        if not name:
            return False, "no scope pass section reads it"
        at = src.get("at") or ""
        base = os.path.basename(at) if at and not at.endswith("}") else ""
        code = code_text(text)
        # an id or a verb only as code — a fenced block or an inline span — never prose ("the board", "health")
        hit = bool(re.search(r"(?<![\w-])%s(?![\w-])" % re.escape(src["id"]), code))
        if src.get("name"):   # a verb as a command: at a word's start, or after a path's slash
            hit = hit or bool(re.search(r"(?:^|[\s/`])%s(?=[\s`]|$)" % re.escape(src["name"]), code, re.M))
        if "." in base:       # a file by its name (TODO.md, fence.log), anywhere; a folder's bare name is a word
            hit = hit or bool(re.search(r"(?<![\w-])%s(?![\w-])" % re.escape(base), text))
        return (True, None) if hit else (False, "the pass section (%s) does not read it yet" % name)
    if reader == PROG:
        return True, None
    return (True, None) if peer(reader) else (False, "its reader %s is not installed" % reader)


def scope_label(name, sc):
    """A scope as every output, record and file name says it: a confidential one by the core's marker."""
    return common.scope_marker(name) if isinstance(sc, dict) and sc.get("confidential") is True else name


def member_sessions(members):
    """path -> True when a transcript is a member's own session: its folder is a member's slug, or a worktree's
    of it, a subagent's under either. Exact, unlike the fence's prefix match (safe for a fence, too wide to count
    a sibling repo's calls as the scope's: round 5)."""
    slugs = {common.project_slug(m) for m in members}

    def match(f):
        f = Path(f)
        folder = f.parent.parent.parent if f.parent.name == "subagents" else f.parent
        return any(folder.name == x or folder.name.startswith(x + "--claude-worktrees-") for x in slugs)
    return match


def _atlas_key(role):
    """(name, Path) from `<config>/atlas/<role>` or `$ATLAS_<ROLE>`, without importing atlas."""
    cfg = Path(common.CONFIG)
    lines = []
    try:
        lines = [l.strip() for l in (cfg / "atlas" / role).read_text(encoding="utf-8-sig").splitlines() if l.strip()]
    except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError):
        pass
    env_var = "ATLAS_%s" % role.upper()
    alt_var = lines[2] if len(lines) > 2 and lines[2].isidentifier() else None
    ov = os.environ.get(env_var) or (os.environ.get(alt_var) if alt_var else None)
    name = lines[0] if lines else role
    if ov:
        return name, Path(ov).expanduser()
    if len(lines) >= 2 and os.path.isabs(os.path.expanduser(lines[1])):
        return name, Path(lines[1]).expanduser()
    if role == "vault" and not (cfg / "regatta" / "overlay").exists():
        return name, Path(os.environ.get("XDG_DATA_HOME") or Path.home() / ".local" / "share").expanduser() / "atlas"
    return name, None


def layer_roots():
    """Forms of the knowledge layer's checkout (`common.overlay_root()` and `atlas/layer`), never hardcoding its name."""
    pts = []
    ov = getattr(common, "overlay_root", lambda: None)()
    if ov:
        pts.append(ov)
    _, lyr = _atlas_key("layer")
    if lyr:
        pts.append(lyr)
    return forms(pts) if pts else set()


def vault_info():
    """(vault Path or None, vault-name) from `atlas/vault` (`$ATLAS_VAULT`)."""
    name, p = _atlas_key("vault")
    return p, name


class Scope:
    """One scope of the registry as coverage reads it: its members' paths, its anchor, its profile — the
    profile checked whole, so a bad value makes the scope's profile_error (never quiet), never a crash.
    S5: `<config>/aurora/scopes/<scope>.json` wins; `<anchor>/.claude/evolve-scope.json` is read only where
    the anchor is neither fenced nor the knowledge layer (a profile placed in the layer is a profile_error);
    the `atlas` scope (or an open scope anchored on the layer) keeps its `evolve/` records in the vault."""

    def __init__(self, name, sc, repos, lens_doc, fenced_by=None, vault=None, layers=None):
        self.name, self.sc = name, sc
        self.confidential = sc.get("confidential") is True
        self.label = scope_label(name, sc)
        keys = common.scope_members(sc, repos)
        self.members = [Path(k) if k.startswith("/") else Path(common.PROJECTS) / k for k in keys]
        ms = sc.get("repos")
        first = ms[0] if isinstance(ms, list) and ms else None
        self.anchor = (Path(first) if first.startswith("/") else Path(common.PROJECTS) / first) \
            if isinstance(first, str) and not common.is_glob(first) else None
        lroots = layer_roots() if layers is None else layers
        self.in_layer = bool(self.anchor is not None and (forms([self.anchor]) & lroots))
        if vault is None and (self.name == "atlas" or self.in_layer):
            vault, _ = vault_info()
        self.vault_records = bool(not self.confidential and (self.name == "atlas" or self.in_layer))
        self.records_home = vault if (self.vault_records and vault is not None) else self.anchor
        # a registry change wakes the scope (finding 7): its own entry and the members it resolves to
        self.reg_sha = hashlib.sha256(json.dumps({"scope": sc, "members": keys}, sort_keys=True).encode()).hexdigest()
        self.refs, self.git_changed, self.sessions_at = {}, False, None
        cfg_prof = Path(common.CONFIG) / "aurora" / "scopes" / ("%s.json" % name)
        anc_prof = (self.anchor / ".claude" / "evolve-scope.json") \
            if (self.anchor is not None and not (fenced_by and fenced_by(self.anchor))) else None
        self.profile_file = cfg_prof
        self.profile, self.profile_error = {}, None
        if self.in_layer and anc_prof is not None and anc_prof.exists():
            self.profile_error = "the profile cannot sit in the knowledge layer (use aurora/scopes/%s.json in the config dir)" % name
            return
        if not cfg_prof.exists() and anc_prof is not None and anc_prof.exists():
            self.profile_file = anc_prof
        if self.profile_file.exists():
            try:
                with open(self.profile_file, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                    prof = json.load(fh)
                why = profile_problem(prof, lens_doc)
                if why:
                    raise ValueError(why)
                self.profile = prof
            except (OSError, ValueError, TypeError) as e:
                detail = type(e).__name__ if not isinstance(e, ValueError) or isinstance(e, json.JSONDecodeError) else str(e)
                self.profile_error = "the profile cannot be read" + ("" if self.confidential else " (%s)" % detail)


def profile_problem(prof, lens_doc):
    if not isinstance(prof, dict):
        return "no object"
    srcs = prof.get("sources") or []
    if not isinstance(srcs, list):
        return "sources is no list"
    own = set()
    for i, s in enumerate(srcs):
        why = source_problem(s, "profile source %d" % (i + 1))
        if why:
            return why
        if not isinstance(s.get("lens"), str) or s["lens"] not in lens_doc["_lens_ids"]:
            return "profile source %d: no lens %r" % (i + 1, s.get("lens"))
        if s["id"] in lens_doc["_source_ids"] or s["id"] in own:   # one id, one cell (finding: ids collide)
            return "profile source %d: id %s is taken" % (i + 1, s["id"])
        if s.get("collector") is not None and s.get("collector") not in {c.get("id") for c in lens_doc.get("collectors") or []}:
            return "profile source %d: no collector %r" % (i + 1, s.get("collector"))   # a typo never drops a requirement
        own.add(s["id"])
    for k, t in (("not_applicable", list), ("exclude", dict), ("conformance", list),
                 ("outcome_classes", dict), ("observation_windows", dict), ("bars", dict), ("radar_queries", list)):
        if prof.get(k) is not None and not isinstance(prof[k], t):
            return "%s is no %s" % (k, t.__name__)
    if any(not isinstance(x, str) for x in prof.get("not_applicable") or []):
        return "not_applicable holds something other than a lens id"
    if any(x not in lens_doc["_lens_ids"] for x in prof.get("not_applicable") or []):
        return "not_applicable names an unknown lens"
    if any(not isinstance(v, dict) for v in (prof.get("exclude") or {}).values()):
        return "an exclusion is no object"
    for oc, spec in (prof.get("outcome_classes") or {}).items():
        if not oc or not isinstance(spec, dict):
            return "outcome_classes[%r] is no object" % oc
        od = spec.get("observation_days")
        if od is not None and (isinstance(od, bool) or not isinstance(od, (int, float)) or od < 0):
            return "outcome_classes[%r]: observation_days is no non-negative number" % oc
    for k, v in (prof.get("observation_windows") or {}).items():
        if isinstance(v, bool) or not isinstance(v, (int, float)) or v < 0:
            return "observation_windows[%r] is no non-negative number" % k
    for ln, b in (prof.get("bars") or {}).items():
        if ln not in lens_doc["_lens_ids"] or not isinstance(b, (str, dict)):
            return "bars[%r]: unknown lens or bad bar" % ln
    if any(not isinstance(q, str) or not q.strip() for q in prof.get("radar_queries") or []):
        return "radar_queries holds a non-string or blank query"
    return None


def expand(at, scope):
    """[(path, root_here)] for a path source's `at`: one per member repo for {repo}, else one."""
    log, cfg = str(common.LOG_DIR), str(common.CONFIG)
    if at.startswith("{repo}"):
        return [(Path(str(m) + at[len("{repo}"):]), m.is_dir()) for m in scope.members]
    if at.startswith("{anchor}"):
        tail = at[len("{anchor}"):]
        if scope.vault_records and scope.records_home is not None and tail.startswith("/evolve"):
            return [(Path(str(scope.records_home) + tail), scope.records_home.is_dir())]
        if scope.vault_records and scope.records_home is not None and tail.startswith("/meetings") and \
                (not scope.anchor or not (scope.anchor / "meetings").exists()) and (scope.records_home / "meetings").exists():
            return [(Path(str(scope.records_home) + tail), scope.records_home.is_dir())]
        return [(Path(str(scope.anchor) + tail), scope.anchor.is_dir())] if scope.anchor else []
    return [(Path(at.replace("{log}", log, 1).replace("{config}", cfg, 1)), True)]


def judge_source(src, scope, fenced_by):
    """{state, stale, change, why} for one source of one scope, before the profile and the reader. A member
    or path of another confidential scope is skipped, never judged; what is left is judged per member, the
    state by `need` (any: the best; all: the worst), its staleness on the freshest member (any) or the
    oldest (all), and its change time on the newest member whatever its rank (finding 2: a commit in any
    member wakes the scope, not only in the first)."""
    kind = src["kind"]
    if kind == "verb":
        ok = peer(src["name"])
        return {"state": "observed" if ok else "source_missing", "stale": None, "change": None,
                "why": None if ok else "the verb %s is not installed" % src["name"]}
    if kind == "git":
        res, need = [], "all"
        kept = [m for m in scope.members if not fenced_by(m)]
        for m in kept:
            if not m.is_dir():
                res.append(("inaccessible", None, "a member repo is not on this host", None))
                continue
            r = git(m, "log", "-1", "--format=%cI")
            t = parse_time(r.stdout.strip()) if r.returncode == 0 and r.stdout.strip() else None
            res.append(("observed", t, None, t) if t else ("source_missing", None, "a member is no git repo with a commit", None))
        fenced = len(kept) < len(scope.members)
    else:
        pairs = expand(src["at"], scope)
        if not pairs:
            return {"state": "source_missing", "stale": None, "change": None, "why": "the scope has no named anchor"}
        kept = [(p, h) for p, h in pairs if not fenced_by(p)]
        res, need, fenced = [judge_path(p, h) for p, h in kept], src.get("need") or "any", len(kept) < len(pairs)
    if not res:
        return {"state": "fenced" if fenced else "source_missing", "stale": None, "change": None,
                "why": "another confidential scope's path" if fenced else "the scope has no member repo"}
    pick = (min if need == "any" else max)(res, key=lambda r: RANK[r[0]])
    times = [t for st, t, _, _ in res if st == "observed" and t]
    now = dt.datetime.now().astimezone()   # a record stamped ahead (a due date, a fast clock) is read as now (round 5)
    res = [(st, min(t, now) if t else t, why, w) for st, t, why, w in res]
    # a change is the write, where a file has one (a record stamped before the cutoff and written after it, or
    # stamped ahead of the clock, judged by when it landed: rounds 3, 5); a folder's time is its newest entry's
    writes = [w or t for st, t, _, w in res if st == "observed" and (t or w)]
    # git's change is scope_state's (the heads, outside the pass's output): a HEAD's commit time would count
    # the pass's own dream once it merges (round 4)
    return {"state": pick[0], "why": pick[2], "change": max(writes) if writes and kind != "git" else None,
            "stale": (max(times) if need == "any" else min(times)) if times else None}


def cited_counts(scope, fenced_by):
    """{source id: findings citing it} over the scope's last four findings files; None when there are none."""
    home = scope.records_home if scope.vault_records else scope.anchor
    d = home / "evolve" if home and not fenced_by(home) else None
    try:   # an unreadable anchor (3.9's is_dir raises EACCES) is no count, never a crash (the finish review)
        files = sorted(d.glob("*.findings.json"))[-4:] if d and d.is_dir() else []
    except OSError:
        return None
    if not files:
        return None
    out = {}
    for f in files:
        try:
            with open(f, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                rec = json.load(fh)
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
        fs = rec.get("findings") if isinstance(rec, dict) else None   # a model wrote it: every shape checked (round 5)
        for fd in fs if isinstance(fs, list) else []:
            refs = fd.get("evidence_refs") if isinstance(fd, dict) else None
            for ref in refs if isinstance(refs, list) else []:
                if isinstance(ref, dict) and isinstance(ref.get("source"), str):
                    out[ref["source"]] = out.get(ref["source"], 0) + 1
    return out


def scope_cells(scope, lens_doc, fenced_by, now):
    prof = scope.profile
    na = set(prof.get("not_applicable") or [])
    excl = prof.get("exclude") or {}
    cited = cited_counts(scope, fenced_by)
    lenses = [dict(ln, sources=list(ln.get("sources") or [])) for ln in lens_doc["lenses"]]
    by_id = {ln["id"]: ln for ln in lenses}
    for i, s in enumerate(prof.get("sources") or []):
        by_id[s["lens"]]["sources"].append(dict(s, _profile=True, _n=i + 1))
    required = {x for c in lens_doc.get("collectors") or [] if c.get("required") for x in c.get("sources") or []} | \
        {s["id"] for s in prof.get("sources") or [] if any(c.get("id") == s.get("collector") and c.get("required")
                                                           for c in lens_doc.get("collectors") or [])}
    cells, extra = [], []
    for ln in lenses:
        for src in ln["sources"]:
            hide = bool(src.get("_profile") and scope.confidential)   # its words never leave: neutral id, reader, why
            sid = "profile-source-%d" % src["_n"] if hide else src["id"]
            reader = src.get("reader")
            cell = {"lens": ln["id"], "source": sid, "outcome": ln.get("outcome"), "stakeholder": ln.get("stakeholder"),
                    "activity": ln.get("activity"),
                    "reader": (reader if reader in (None, "pass", PROG) else "tool") if hide else reader,
                    "age_days": None, "cited": None if cited is None else cited.get(src["id"], 0), "owner_read": None,
                    "required": src["id"] in required, "why": None}
            j = {"change": None}
            if ln["id"] in na:
                cell.update(state="not_applicable", why="the profile says so")
            elif src["id"] in excl:
                x = excl[src["id"]] if isinstance(excl[src["id"]], dict) else {}
                review = valid_day(x.get("review"))
                overdue = not review or review < now.date().isoformat()
                cell.update(state="excluded", review=review, overdue=bool(overdue),
                            why=("excluded, its review " + ("overdue" if overdue else "on %s" % review)) if scope.confidential
                            else "%s (review %s%s)" % (x.get("reason") or "no reason given", review or "none", ", overdue" if overdue else ""))
            else:
                j = judge_source(src, scope, fenced_by)
                state, why = j["state"], j["why"]
                if state == "observed":
                    ok, rwhy = reader_here(src, scope, fenced_by)
                    if not ok:
                        state, why = "unread", rwhy
                    elif j["stale"] is not None and src.get("fresh_days") is not None:
                        age = (now - j["stale"]).total_seconds() / 86400
                        if age > float(src["fresh_days"]):
                            state, why = "stale", "%.0f days old, fresh within %s" % (age, src["fresh_days"])
                if j["stale"] is not None:
                    cell["age_days"] = round(max(0.0, (now - j["stale"]).total_seconds() / 86400), 1)
                cell.update(state=state, why=NEUTRAL.get(state) if hide and why else why)
            cells.append(cell)
            # the scope's own: its repos, and whatever its profile declares for it alone (round 2: a misfire log)
            own = src["kind"] == "git" or bool(src.get("_profile")) or str(src.get("at") or "").startswith(OWN_ROOTS)
            extra.append({"id": src["id"], "cell": sid, "kind": src["kind"], "collector": src.get("collector"),
                          "change": j["change"], "wakes": bool(src.get("wakes", own)), "fresh_days": src.get("fresh_days")})
    return cells, extra


PASS_OUTPUT = (":!dreams/", ":!evolve/")   # what the pass itself writes into its anchor: never a change to it


def scope_state(scope, fenced_by, base, current=None):
    """Two values a quiet receipt may not sleep through (rounds 2, 3). The members' branch heads, as values:
    against the baseline's heads, a change is a commit reachable now and not then that touches anything but
    the pass's own output (the anchor's `dreams/` and `evolve/`; every other member's whole tree), so a fast-forward of old commits or a worktree's branch
    wakes the scope and the pass's records branch, or its merge, does not. And the newest time a session of
    the scope wrote its transcript (stat only, never opened), the pass's own session (--promote --session)
    left out; a folder is the member's own (its slug, or a worktree's), never a sibling repo's that shares a
    prefix."""
    base_refs = (base or {}).get("refs") if isinstance((base or {}).get("refs"), dict) else None
    # a baseline with no heads to compare is a change, never "git is not judged" (the finish review)
    scope.refs, scope.git_changed = {}, bool(base) and base_refs is None
    for m in scope.members:
        if fenced_by(m) or not m.is_dir():
            continue
        r = git(m, "for-each-ref", "--format=%(objectname)", "refs/heads")
        heads = sorted(set(r.stdout.split())) if r.returncode == 0 else []
        key = hashlib.sha256(str(m).encode()).hexdigest()[:16]   # no repo's path in the manifest file (round 4)
        scope.refs[key] = heads
        if base_refs is None:
            continue
        old = base_refs.get(key)
        new = [h for h in heads if h not in (old or [])]
        if old is None:
            scope.git_changed = True
        elif new:
            pass_homes = {os.path.realpath(x) for x in (scope.anchor, scope.records_home) if x is not None}
            outside = PASS_OUTPUT if os.path.realpath(m) in pass_homes else ()
            q = git(m, "rev-list", "--max-count=1", *new, "--not", *old, "--", ".", *outside)
            if q.returncode != 0 or q.stdout.strip():
                scope.git_changed = True
    skip = {(base or {}).get("pass_session"), current} - {None}   # the last pass's session and this one's
    newest = 0.0
    for d in common.login_dirs():
        root = d / "projects"
        for m in scope.members:
            if fenced_by(m):
                continue
            slug = common.project_slug(m)
            for folder in [root / slug] + sorted(root.glob(globmod.escape(slug) + "--claude-worktrees-*")):
                if fenced_by(folder):
                    continue
                for f in folder.glob("*.jsonl"):
                    if f.stem in skip:
                        continue
                    try:
                        newest = max(newest, f.stat().st_mtime)
                    except OSError:
                        continue
    scope.sessions_at = dt.datetime.fromtimestamp(newest).astimezone() if newest else None


def label_path(label, suffix):
    return state_dir() / "manifests" / ("%s%s.json" % (label.replace(":", "-"), suffix))


def label_file(scope, suffix):
    return label_path(scope.label, suffix)


def verb_receipt(scope, cell_id, now, days):
    """A verb collector's run receipt, `<state>/receipts/<scope>/<cell's source id>.json` {"time"} (a confidential
    scope's profile source by its neutral id), which the pass writes
    when it ran the verb (S5): an installed verb that never ran is no fresh collector (finding 9)."""
    try:
        with open(state_dir() / "receipts" / scope.label.replace(":", "-") / ("%s.json" % cell_id), encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            t = parse_time((json.load(fh) or {}).get("time"))
    except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError):
        return False
    return bool(t) and (now - t).total_seconds() <= float(days) * 86400


def read_baseline(scope):
    """The last complete pass's manifest, or None."""
    try:
        with open(label_file(scope, ".complete"), encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            b = json.load(fh)
        return b if isinstance(b, dict) else None
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None


def manifest(scope, lens_doc, cells, extra, now, since, base):
    """The collector manifest a quiet receipt rests on, against the last COMPLETE pass's (finding 6: a run
    that only looked moves nothing): every required collector's sources seen fresh (a verb with its run
    receipt), no change in lenses.json, the profile, the North Star or the scope's registry entry, no record
    newer than the baseline's cutoff in a source that wakes the scope, no exclusion past its review."""
    cell_of = {e["id"]: c for e, c in zip(extra, cells)}
    ex = {e["id"]: e for e in extra}
    cols = [dict(c) for c in lens_doc.get("collectors") or []]
    for e in extra:   # a profile source joins the collector it names
        for c in cols:
            if e["collector"] == c.get("id"):
                c["sources"] = list(c.get("sources") or []) + [e["id"]]
    out_cols, why = [], []
    for c in cols:
        bad = []
        for sid in c.get("sources") or []:
            cell = cell_of.get(sid)
            st = cell["state"] if cell else "source_missing"
            name = ex[sid]["cell"] if sid in ex else sid
            if not (st in ("observed", "not_applicable") or (st == "excluded" and not cell.get("overdue"))):
                bad.append("%s %s" % (name, st))
            elif st == "observed" and ex[sid]["kind"] == "verb" and \
                    not verb_receipt(scope, name, now, ex[sid]["fresh_days"] or VERB_RECEIPT_DAYS):
                bad.append("%s no run receipt" % name)
        out_cols.append({"id": c["id"], "required": bool(c.get("required")), "sources": [ex[s]["cell"] if s in ex else s for s in c.get("sources") or []],
                         "fresh": not bad, "why": "; ".join(bad) or None})
        if c.get("required") and bad:
            why.append("collector %s: %s" % (c["id"], "; ".join(bad)))
    hashes = {"lenses": lens_doc["_sha"], "profile": file_sha(scope.profile_file),
              "north_star": file_sha(Path(common.CONFIG) / "sextant" / "north-star.json"), "registry": scope.reg_sha}
    changed = ["no complete pass yet"] if not isinstance(base, dict) else \
        [k for k in hashes if (base.get("hashes") or {}).get(k) != hashes[k]] + (["git"] if scope.git_changed else [])
    if since is None and isinstance(base, dict):
        since = base.get("cutoff")
    st = parse_time(since) if since else None
    if since and st is None:
        why.append("the baseline's cutoff cannot be read")
    changed_sources = sorted({e["cell"] for e in extra if st and e["wakes"] and e["change"] and e["change"] > st} |
                             ({"sessions"} if st and scope.sessions_at and scope.sessions_at > st else set()))
    overdue = [c["source"] for c in cells if c.get("overdue")]
    if scope.profile_error:
        why.append(scope.profile_error)
    if changed:
        why.append("changed: " + ", ".join(changed))
    if changed_sources:
        why.append("new records since the last complete pass: " + ", ".join(changed_sources))
    if overdue:
        why.append("an exclusion past its review: " + ", ".join(overdue))
    # the cutoff to the microsecond: a file written in the same second after it is a change (its mtime is finer)
    return {"scope": scope.label, "cutoff": now.isoformat(timespec="microseconds"), "since": since,
            "collectors": out_cols, "hashes": hashes, "refs": scope.refs, "changed": changed, "changed_sources": changed_sources,
            "overdue": overdue, "quiet_ok": not why, "why": why,
            "not_judged": ["a due benefit check (the grader, S9)", "whether the owner read a source"]}


def forms(paths):
    """Each path as given (normalised) and resolved: a source named through a link is read either way."""
    out = set()
    for p in paths:
        out.add(os.path.normpath(os.path.abspath(str(p))))
        out.add(os.path.realpath(str(p)))
    return out


def surface(reg, scopes, lens_doc, fenced_by, now):
    """The surface diff: every registry repo, each entry of the log dir and the config dir, minus what any
    declared source reads (a source inside an entry opens it one level down, to three). A confidential
    scope's path is counted, never named; an ignore glob (lenses.json, or the overlay's
    <config>/aurora/surface.json with a reason and a review date, past which it lapses) drops an item."""
    member_keys = set()
    repos = reg.get("repos") or {}
    for sc in (reg.get("scopes") or {}).values():
        member_keys |= set(common.scope_members(sc, repos))
    read, secret = set(), set()
    for scope in scopes:
        for ln in lens_doc["lenses"]:
            for src in list(ln.get("sources") or []) + [s for s in scope.profile.get("sources") or [] if s.get("lens") == ln["id"]]:
                if src["kind"] == "path":
                    paths = forms(p for p, _ in expand(src["at"], scope))
                    # a confidential profile's own paths name its folders: fenced, counted, never named (round 2)
                    (secret if scope.confidential and src in (scope.profile.get("sources") or []) else read).update(paths)
    torn = any(sc.confidential and sc.profile_error for sc in scopes)   # its folders unknown: name no entry
    cfg = Path(common.CONFIG)
    read |= forms((cfg / "aurora" / "scopes", cfg / "aurora" / "surface.json", cfg / "aurora" / "conformance.json",
                   cfg / "atlas", cfg / "sextant" / "north-star.json", state_dir()) + ((common.repos_json(),) if common.repos_json() else ()))
    ignore = list((lens_doc.get("surface") or {}).get("ignore") or [])
    try:
        with open(cfg / "aurora" / "surface.json", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            ign = json.load(fh).get("ignore")
            for x in ign if isinstance(ign, list) else []:
                if isinstance(x, dict) and isinstance(x.get("glob"), str) and (valid_day(x.get("review")) or "") >= now.date().isoformat():
                    ignore.append(x["glob"])
    except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError):
        pass
    items, unobserved, fenced, ignored = 0, [], 0, 0

    def walk(root, tag, rel, depth):
        nonlocal items, fenced, ignored
        p = root / rel if rel else root
        try:
            kids = sorted(p.iterdir()) if p.is_dir() else []
        except OSError:
            kids = []
        for k in kids:
            name = "%s:%s" % (tag, k.relative_to(root))
            if any(fnmatch.fnmatchcase(name, g) for g in ignore):
                ignored += 1
                continue
            ks = forms([k])
            if fenced_by(k) or any(x == r or x.startswith(r + os.sep) or r.startswith(x + os.sep) for x in ks for r in secret):
                fenced += 1
                continue
            if ks & read or any(x.startswith(r + os.sep) for x in ks for r in read):
                items += 1
                continue
            inside = [r for r in read for x in ks if r.startswith(x + os.sep)]
            # never through a link: the config dir links synced cloud folders, and listing one fetches it (AGENTS.md)
            if inside and depth < 3 and k.is_dir() and not k.is_symlink():
                walk(root, tag, k.relative_to(root), depth + 1)
                continue
            items += 1
            if not inside:
                if torn:
                    fenced += 1
                else:
                    unobserved.append(name)
    for key in sorted(repos):
        if fenced_by(Path(key) if key.startswith("/") else Path(common.PROJECTS) / key):
            fenced += 1
            continue
        items += 1
        if key not in member_keys:
            unobserved.append("repo:%s" % key)
    roots = {"log": Path(common.LOG_DIR), "config": cfg}
    for tag in (lens_doc.get("surface") or {}).get("roots") or ["log", "config"]:
        if tag in roots:
            walk(roots[tag], tag, None, 1)
    return {"items": items, "unobserved": unobserved, "fenced": fenced, "ignored": ignored}


def registry_or_refusal():
    """(reg, None) from one parse of the registry, or (None, why): an unreadable one fails closed, and no
    registry is no scope to walk. Every scope is walked from this one read (AGENTS.md's fence traps)."""
    reg, bad = common.read_registry()
    if bad:
        return None, "the registry cannot be read: every scope is fenced, nothing judged"
    if reg is None:
        return None, "no registry: no scope to walk"
    return reg, None


def matchers(reg):
    """{name: matcher} for every confidential scope, built once from the one registry read: every scope
    walked, never the first that lists a repo."""
    return {n: common.scope_match(n, reg=reg) for n in common.confidential_scopes(reg=reg)}


def fence_for(ms, own=None):
    """path -> True when it is a confidential scope's other than OWN."""
    others = [m for n, m in ms.items() if n != own]
    return lambda p: any(m(p) for m in others)


def cmd_coverage(a):
    try:
        lens_doc = load_lenses()
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        raise Refused("lenses.json cannot be read (%s)" % e)
    if a.since and schema.read_time(a.since) is None:   # a time, as the manifest's schema reads it: a bare date is none
        raise Refused("--since %r is no ISO time (a date and a time)" % a.since)
    if a.promote and not a.scope:
        raise Refused("--promote names the scope whose pass completed (--scope)")
    if a.promote and (a.no_record or a.open):
        raise Refused("--promote writes the baseline: never with --no-record or --open")
    if a.session and not (a.promote or a.open):
        raise Refused("--session names the pass's own session, with --open or --promote, and nothing else")
    if a.open and (not a.scope or a.no_record):
        raise Refused("--open is the pass's opening run: with --scope, recorded")
    if a.promote:
        return promote(a)
    reg, why = registry_or_refusal()
    if why:
        raise Refused(why)
    names = sorted(reg.get("scopes") or {})
    if a.scope and a.scope not in names:
        raise Refused("no scope %r in the registry" % a.scope)
    if a.scope and not isinstance(reg["scopes"][a.scope], dict):
        raise Refused("scope %r in the registry is no object: nothing to judge" % a.scope)
    def usable(x):   # an object whose `repos` is a list: anything else names nothing to judge (round 4)
        return isinstance(x, dict) and isinstance(x.get("repos"), list)
    if a.scope and not usable(reg["scopes"][a.scope]):
        raise Refused("scope %r in the registry has no list of repos: nothing to judge" % a.scope)
    bad_scopes = sum(1 for n in names if not usable(reg["scopes"][n]))
    now = dt.datetime.now().astimezone()
    repos = reg.get("repos") or {}
    ms = matchers(reg)
    vpath, _ = vault_info()
    lroots = layer_roots()
    scopes = [Scope(n, reg["scopes"][n], repos, lens_doc, fenced_by=fence_for(ms, own=n), vault=vpath, layers=lroots)
              for n in names if usable(reg["scopes"][n])]
    result = {"version": 1, "time": now.isoformat(timespec="seconds"), "lenses_sha": lens_doc["_sha"], "scopes": [],
              "surface": {"items": 0, "unobserved": [], "fenced": 0, "ignored": 0}, "bad_scopes": 0 if a.scope else bad_scopes,
              "skipped_confidential": 0}
    for sc in scopes:
        if a.scope and sc.name != a.scope:
            continue
        if sc.confidential and not a.scope:
            # what leaves a confidential scope is its checked lines and the receipt word, nothing else (the
            # scope-pass component): a global run neither opens its anchor nor records its ages, wakes or
            # citations; its pass judges it under its own --scope (the finish review)
            result["skipped_confidential"] += 1
            continue
        own_fence = fence_for(ms, own=sc.name)
        base = read_baseline(sc)
        cells, extra = scope_cells(sc, lens_doc, own_fence, now)
        scope_state(sc, own_fence, base, a.session)
        counts = {}
        for c in cells:
            counts[c["state"]] = counts.get(c["state"], 0) + 1
        m = manifest(sc, lens_doc, cells, extra, now, a.since, base)
        if a.session:
            m["pass_session"] = a.session
        # the global record keeps no heads, and of a confidential scope no hash a guess could be confirmed against
        rec = {k: v for k, v in m.items() if k != "refs"}
        if sc.confidential:
            rec["hashes"] = {k: v for k, v in m["hashes"].items() if k in ("lenses", "north_star")}
        result["scopes"].append({"scope": sc.label, "confidential": sc.confidential, "counts": counts, "cells": cells,
                                 "manifest": rec, "profile_error": bool(sc.profile_error)})
        if not a.no_record:
            try:
                label_file(sc, "").parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
                for suffix in ("", ".opening") if a.open else ("",):
                    with open(label_file(sc, suffix), "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                        json.dump(m, fh, indent=1)
            except OSError as e:
                print("%s coverage: the manifest could not be written (%s)" % (PROG, e), file=sys.stderr)
    if not a.scope:
        result["surface"] = surface(reg, scopes, lens_doc, fence_for(ms), now)
    if not a.no_record:
        append_record("coverage.jsonl", result)
    blind = [c for s in result["scopes"] for c in s["cells"] if c["state"] in NOT_SEEN] + result["surface"]["unobserved"] + \
        ["a profile" for s in result["scopes"] if s["profile_error"]] + ["a scope entry"] * result["bad_scopes"] + \
        [c for s in result["scopes"] for c in s["cells"] if c.get("overdue")]   # an overdue cell (the finish review)
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps(result, indent=1))
    else:
        for s in result["scopes"]:
            print("scope %s: %s" % (s["scope"], ", ".join("%d %s" % (n, k) for k, n in sorted(s["counts"].items()))))
            for c in s["cells"]:
                if c["state"] not in ("observed", "not_applicable"):
                    print("  %-14s %s/%s — %s" % (c["state"], c["lens"], c["source"], c["why"] or ""))
            m = s["manifest"]
            if s["profile_error"]:
                print("  profile        unreadable: its sources not judged")
            print("  quiet: %s" % ("allowed" if m["quiet_ok"] else "not allowed — " + "; ".join(m["why"])))
        if result["skipped_confidential"]:
            n = result["skipped_confidential"]
            print("%d confidential scope%s judged only inside it (--scope)" % (n, "" if n == 1 else "s"))
        if not a.scope:
            sf = result["surface"]
            print("surface: %d items, %d nothing reads%s%s" % (sf["items"], len(sf["unobserved"]),
                  ", %d of a confidential scope (counted, not named)" % sf["fenced"] if sf["fenced"] else "",
                  ", %d ignored" % sf["ignored"] if sf["ignored"] else ""))
            for u in sf["unobserved"]:
                print("  unobserved     %s" % u)
        if result["bad_scopes"]:
            print("%d registry scope%s no object: not judged" % (result["bad_scopes"], " is" if result["bad_scopes"] == 1 else "s are"))
        print("coverage: %s" % ("every cell observed" if not blind else "%d blind spot%s" % (len(blind), "" if len(blind) == 1 else "s")))
    return 0 if not blind else 1


def promote(a):
    """The pass completed: the manifest its opening run wrote (`coverage --scope S --open`, a file no other run
    writes, so a run in between moves nothing: round 3) becomes the scope's baseline, its cutoff, hashes and
    heads as the pass saw them — never this moment's, so what landed while the pass ran is still a change next
    time (round 2). --session names the pass's own session, whose transcript is then no change."""
    reg, why = registry_or_refusal()
    if why:
        raise Refused(why)
    if a.scope not in (reg.get("scopes") or {}) or not isinstance(reg["scopes"][a.scope], dict):
        raise Refused("no scope %r in the registry" % a.scope)
    sc = reg["scopes"][a.scope]
    label = scope_label(a.scope, sc)
    src = label_path(label, ".opening")
    try:
        with open(src, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            m = json.load(fh)
        if schema.validate("manifest", m):
            raise ValueError("it does not hold its schema")
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        raise Refused("no manifest of the pass's opening run to promote (%s): run `coverage --scope %s --open` as the pass starts"
                      % (type(e).__name__ if isinstance(e, OSError) else e, label))
    if a.session:
        m["pass_session"] = a.session   # its own transcript is no change to the next run (else the opening run's)
    with open(label_path(label, ".complete"), "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        json.dump(m, fh, indent=1)
    print("%s coverage: %s's baseline is the pass's, cut off %s" % (PROG, label, m.get("cutoff")))
    return 0


def append_record(name, obj):
    d = state_dir()
    try:
        d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        with open(d / name, "a", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            fh.write(json.dumps(obj) + "\n")
        return d / name
    except OSError as e:
        print("%s: the record could not be written (%s)" % (PROG, e), file=sys.stderr)
        return None


# ---- conformance: work-as-imagined (rules) against work-as-done (the transcripts' tool calls) ----------

# a guard's refusal as Claude Code writes it into the tool result (read from transcripts, S3's review): a
# PreToolUse hook's ("PreToolUse:Bash hook error: ⛔ …", whatever the words after) or the permission system's
HOOK_DENIAL = re.compile(r"\s*PreToolUse:\S+ hook error")
PERMISSION_DENIAL = re.compile(r"\s*(?:Permission to use \S+ .*?has been denied|Permission for this (?:action|command) was denied by"
                               r"|The user doesn't want to proceed with this tool use)", re.S)
NO_VERDICT = re.compile(r"\s*The server-side auto mode classifier gave no verdict")   # never ran: neither ok nor failed


def load_rules(rules, where, named=True):
    """[rule] from a list of {id, ref, tool, when, breach}, each regex compiled; ValueError naming the bad one
    (by its place, never its id, where NAMED is false: a confidential scope's rule)."""
    out = []
    for i, r in enumerate(rules if isinstance(rules, list) else []):
        tag = "rule %s" % (r.get("id") if named and isinstance(r, dict) else i + 1)
        if not isinstance(r, dict) or not r.get("id") or not (r.get("when") or r.get("breach")):
            raise ValueError("%s, rule %d: needs an id and a `when` or a `breach`" % (where, i + 1))
        try:
            out.append(dict(r, _tool=re.compile(r.get("tool") or r"^Bash$"),
                            _when=re.compile(r["when"]) if r.get("when") else None,
                            _breach=re.compile(r["breach"]) if r.get("breach") else None))
        except (re.error, TypeError) as e:
            raise ValueError("%s, %s: a pattern does not compile (%s)" % (where, tag, e))
    return out


def transcripts(since):
    """Every transcript in every login dir touched since SINCE — the sessions' own and their subagents', where
    workers run most of the shell (S3's review) — each file once by its real path (login dirs may link one
    projects folder: round 2), the file's mtime only prefiltering; the events' times decide."""
    seen = set()
    for d in common.login_dirs():
        for pat in ("*/*.jsonl", "*/*/subagents/*.jsonl"):
            for f in sorted((d / "projects").glob(pat)):
                try:
                    real = os.path.realpath(f)
                    if real in seen or f.stat().st_mtime < since.timestamp():
                        continue
                    seen.add(real)
                    yield f
                except OSError:
                    continue


def result_text(body):
    if isinstance(body, str):
        return body
    if isinstance(body, list):
        return "\n".join(x.get("text", "") for x in body if isinstance(x, dict) and isinstance(x.get("text"), str))
    return ""


def tool_calls(f, since):
    """[(name, text, session, ok, denied)] — each tool call at or after SINCE, with its result: denied only
    for an error result in a guard's shape, so a call that succeeded never counts as blocked."""
    uses, results = [], {}
    with open(f, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as fh:
        for line in fh:
            if '"tool_use"' not in line and '"tool_result"' not in line:
                continue   # most lines are text: only a tool call or its result is read
            try:
                ev = json.loads(line)
            except ValueError:
                continue
            msg = ev.get("message") if isinstance(ev, dict) else None
            content = msg.get("content") if isinstance(msg, dict) else None
            if not isinstance(content, list):
                continue
            for c in content:
                if not isinstance(c, dict):
                    continue
                if c.get("type") == "tool_use" and ev.get("type") == "assistant":
                    t = parse_time(ev.get("timestamp")) if ev.get("timestamp") else None
                    if t is None or t < since:
                        continue
                    inp = c.get("input") if isinstance(c.get("input"), dict) else {}
                    text = inp.get("command") if isinstance(inp.get("command"), str) else json.dumps(inp, sort_keys=True)
                    uses.append((c.get("id"), c.get("name") or "", text, ev.get("sessionId") or f.stem))
                elif c.get("type") == "tool_result":
                    err, body = bool(c.get("is_error")), result_text(c.get("content"))
                    outcome = "ok" if not err else "denied" if HOOK_DENIAL.match(body) or PERMISSION_DENIAL.match(body) \
                        else "unknown" if NO_VERDICT.match(body) else "failed"
                    results[c.get("tool_use_id")] = outcome
    # [(id, name, text, session, outcome)]: no result read is `unknown`, never a success nor a failure
    return [(uid, name, text, sess, results.get(uid, "unknown")) for uid, name, text, sess in uses]


def cmd_conformance(a):
    try:
        lens_doc = load_lenses()
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        raise Refused("lenses.json cannot be read (%s)" % e)
    conf = lens_doc.get("conformance") or {}
    reg, why = registry_or_refusal()
    if why:
        raise Refused(why)
    scopes_reg = reg.get("scopes") or {}
    if a.scope and a.scope not in scopes_reg:
        raise Refused("no scope %r in the registry" % a.scope)
    rules_file = Path(common.CONFIG) / "aurora" / "conformance.json"
    ms = matchers(reg)
    vpath, _ = vault_info()
    lroots = layer_roots()
    groups, skipped, unreadable = [], 0, 0   # (scope name or None, [rule])
    try:
        if rules_file.exists():
            with open(rules_file, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                groups.append((None, load_rules(json.load(fh).get("rules"), "conformance.json")))
        for n in sorted(scopes_reg):
            if a.scope and n != a.scope:
                continue
            if not (isinstance(scopes_reg[n], dict) and isinstance(scopes_reg[n].get("repos"), list)):
                if a.scope == n:
                    raise ValueError("scope %s in the registry has no list of repos" % n)
                unreadable += 1   # nothing to judge its rules on
                continue
            sc = Scope(n, scopes_reg[n], reg.get("repos") or {}, lens_doc, fenced_by=fence_for(ms, own=n), vault=vpath, layers=lroots)
            if sc.profile_error:
                if a.scope == n:
                    raise ValueError("scope %s: %s" % (sc.label, sc.profile_error))
                unreadable += 1   # another scope's profile: its rules unknown, the rest still judged
                continue
            if not sc.profile.get("conformance"):
                continue
            if sc.confidential and a.scope != n:
                skipped += 1   # its transcripts are fenced here: its rules are judged inside, under --scope
                continue
            try:
                groups.append((n, load_rules(sc.profile["conformance"], "scope %s's profile" % sc.label, named=not sc.confidential)))
            except ValueError:
                if a.scope == n:
                    raise
                unreadable += 1   # another scope's bad rule: its rules unknown, the rest still judged (the finish review)
    except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError) as e:
        raise Refused(str(e))
    now = dt.datetime.now().astimezone()
    since = now - dt.timedelta(days=a.days)
    ms = matchers(reg)
    others = fence_for(ms, own=a.scope)
    def members(n):
        return [Path(k) if k.startswith("/") else Path(common.PROJECTS) / k for k in common.scope_members(scopes_reg[n], reg.get("repos") or {})]
    own = member_sessions(members(a.scope)) if a.scope else None
    scope_m = {n: member_sessions(members(n)) for n, _ in groups if n}
    calls, read, fenced, ids = [], 0, 0, {}
    for f in transcripts(since) if groups else ():
        if others(f):
            fenced += 1
            continue   # judged on the path before any open (the S1 trap)
        if own and not own(f):
            continue
        read += 1
        try:
            for c in tool_calls(f, since):
                if c[0] and c[0] in ids:   # a resumed or forked session carries the same call: counted once,
                    i = ids[c[0]]          # with the outcome a copy knows over one that has no result
                    if calls[i][-1] == "unknown" and c[-1] != "unknown":
                        calls[i] = (f,) + c[1:]
                    continue
                if c[0]:
                    ids[c[0]] = len(calls)
                calls.append((f,) + c[1:])
        except OSError:
            continue
    rows = []
    for n, rules in groups:
        conf_scope = bool(n) and scopes_reg[n].get("confidential") is True
        inside = {f: scope_m[n](f) for f in {c[0] for c in calls}} if n else None   # once a file, not once a rule
        for i, r in enumerate(rules):
            applied = ok = failed = blocked = unknown = 0
            ok_sessions = set()
            for f, name, text, sess, outcome in calls:
                if n and not inside[f]:
                    continue
                if not r["_tool"].search(name):
                    continue
                hit = bool(r["_when"] and r["_when"].search(text))
                br = bool(r["_breach"] and r["_breach"].search(text))
                if not (hit or br):
                    continue
                applied += 1
                if br:
                    if outcome == "denied":
                        blocked += 1
                    elif outcome == "ok":
                        ok += 1
                        ok_sessions.add(sess)
                    elif outcome == "failed":
                        failed += 1
                    else:
                        unknown += 1
            cls = "dead" if not applied else "worked_around" if ok >= int(conf.get("workaround_min", 3)) and \
                len(ok_sessions) >= int(conf.get("workaround_sessions", 2)) else "violated" if ok or failed \
                else "unknown" if unknown else "holds"   # holds: no breach, or every one refused; unmeasured is not
            rid = "%s/rule-%d" % (common.scope_marker(n), i + 1) if conf_scope else ("%s/%s" % (n, r["id"]) if n else r["id"])
            rows.append({"rule": rid, "class": cls, "applied": applied, "breached_ok": ok, "breached_failed": failed,
                         "blocked": blocked, "unknown": unknown, "sessions": len(ok_sessions), "ref": None if conf_scope else r.get("ref")})
    result = {"time": now.isoformat(timespec="seconds"), "days": a.days,
              "scope": (common.scope_marker(a.scope) if scopes_reg[a.scope].get("confidential") is True else a.scope) if a.scope else None,
              "transcripts": read, "fenced": fenced, "skipped_confidential": skipped, "unreadable_profiles": unreadable, "rules": rows}
    if not a.no_record:
        append_record("conformance.jsonl", {**result, "rules": [{k: v for k, v in r.items() if k != "ref"} for r in rows]})
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps(result, indent=1))
    else:
        print("%d transcript%s read over %d days%s" % (read, "" if read == 1 else "s", a.days,
              "; %d of a confidential scope fenced, never opened" % fenced if fenced else ""))
        if skipped:
            print("%d confidential scope%s' rules judged only inside it (--scope)" % (skipped, "" if skipped == 1 else "s"))
        if unreadable:
            print("%d scope profile%s could not be read: %s rules not judged" % (unreadable, "" if unreadable == 1 else "s", "their" if unreadable > 1 else "its"))
        if not rows:
            print("no rules: declare them in %s or a scope's profile (`conformance`)" % rules_file)
        for r in rows:
            print("  %-13s %s — applied %d, breached %d ok %d failed, %d blocked by a guard, %d session%s%s" % (
                r["class"], r["rule"], r["applied"], r["breached_ok"], r["breached_failed"], r["blocked"],
                r["sessions"], "" if r["sessions"] == 1 else "s", " (%s)" % r["ref"] if r.get("ref") else ""))
        n_bad = sum(1 for r in rows if r["class"] != "holds")
        print("conformance: %s" % ("no rules declared" if not rows else "every rule holds" if not n_bad
                                   else "%d rule%s dead, violated or worked around" % (n_bad, "" if n_bad == 1 else "s")))
    return 0 if rows and all(r["class"] == "holds" for r in rows) else 1


def _classes_for_scope(sname, base_classes, doc, explicit=False):
    out = dict(base_classes or {})
    if not sname:
        return out
    reg, bad = common.read_registry()
    if bad or reg is None:
        if explicit:
            raise Refused("the registry cannot be read")
        return out
    scopes_reg = reg.get("scopes") or {}
    target = sname if sname in scopes_reg else next(
        (n for n, v in scopes_reg.items() if isinstance(v, dict) and scope_label(n, v) == sname), None)
    if not target or not isinstance(scopes_reg.get(target), dict) or not isinstance(scopes_reg[target].get("repos"), list):
        if explicit:
            raise Refused("no usable scope %r in the registry" % sname)
        return out
    ms = matchers(reg)
    vpath, _ = vault_info()
    sc = Scope(target, scopes_reg[target], reg.get("repos") or {}, doc, fenced_by=fence_for(ms, own=target), vault=vpath)
    if sc.profile_error:
        if explicit:
            raise Refused("scope %s: %s" % (sc.label, sc.profile_error))
        return out
    if isinstance(sc.profile.get("outcome_classes"), dict):
        out.update(sc.profile["outcome_classes"])
    return out


def cmd_validate(a):
    if a.kind not in schema.SCHEMAS:
        print("%s validate: no schema %r (one of %s)" % (PROG, a.kind, ", ".join(sorted(schema.SCHEMAS))), file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    try:
        with open(a.file, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            raw = fh.read()
    except OSError as e:
        print("%s validate: %s" % (PROG, e), file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    try:
        doc = load_lenses() if a.kind in ("finding", "findings") else {}
        base_classes, lens_ids = doc.get("outcome_classes"), set(doc.get("_lens_ids") or [])
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        raise Refused("a finding's outcome class is judged against lenses.json, which cannot be read (%s)" % e)
    explicit_classes = _classes_for_scope(getattr(a, "scope", None), base_classes, doc, explicit=True) if getattr(a, "scope", None) else None
    recs = []
    if a.file.endswith(".jsonl"):
        for n, line in enumerate(raw.splitlines(), 1):
            if line.strip():
                try:
                    recs.append(("line %d" % n, json.loads(line)))
                except ValueError:
                    recs.append(("line %d" % n, ValueError("not JSON")))
    else:
        try:
            d = json.loads(raw)
        except ValueError:
            d = ValueError("not JSON")
        recs = [(k, v) for k, v in d.items()] if a.kind == "theme" and isinstance(d, dict) else [("", d)]
    bad = 0
    for where, rec in recs:
        classes = explicit_classes
        if classes is None and a.kind in ("finding", "findings") and isinstance(rec, dict):
            classes = _classes_for_scope(rec.get("scope"), base_classes, doc, explicit=False) if rec.get("scope") else base_classes
        probs = [str(rec)] if isinstance(rec, ValueError) else schema.validate(a.kind, rec, classes)
        if lens_ids and not isinstance(rec, ValueError):   # a lens lenses.json never declared (the finish review)
            fs = [rec] if a.kind == "finding" else (rec.get("findings") if isinstance(rec, dict) else None)
            for i, f in enumerate(fs if isinstance(fs, list) else []):
                ln = f.get("lens") if isinstance(f, dict) else None
                if isinstance(ln, str) and ln and ln not in lens_ids:
                    probs.append("%slens: %r is no lens lenses.json declares" % ("" if a.kind == "finding" else "findings[%d]." % i, ln))
        for p in probs:
            print("%s%s" % ("%s: " % where if where else "", p))
        bad += bool(probs)
    if not a.quiet:
        print("%s: %d record%s, %s" % (a.kind, len(recs), "" if len(recs) == 1 else "s", "all hold" if not bad else "%d refused" % bad))
    return 0 if not bad and recs else 1


def cmd_schema(a):
    if not a.kind:
        print("\n".join(sorted(schema.SCHEMAS)))
        return 0
    if a.kind not in schema.SCHEMAS:
        print("%s schema: no schema %r" % (PROG, a.kind), file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    print(json.dumps(schema.describe(a.kind), indent=1))
    return 0


def cmd_action_id(a):
    print(schema.action_id(a.finding_id, a.action_version, a.target_scope))
    return 0


# ---- S5: the scope pass in shadow: where, open, critic, record, meetings, replay, shadow ----------------

CRITIC_SITE = "evolve.critic"
SENSOR_RX = re.compile(r"\b(sensor|probe|probes|collector|coverage|log|jsonl|json|check|schedule|scheduled|cron|metric|ledger|verb|hook|test|watch|monitor)\b", re.I)
TRIVIAL_CHECK = {"none", "manual", "tbd", "todo", "n/a", "na", "unknown"}
RECORDING_EXTS = (".vtt", ".srt", ".m4a", ".mp3", ".wav", ".mp4", ".mov", ".eml", ".ics")
IF_THEN_RX = re.compile(r"^\s*[-*]\s+(?:If\b.+?\bthen\b.+|.+)", re.I)
DUE_RX = re.compile(r"\bdue:\s*(\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2})\b", re.I)
CONFIRMED_RX = re.compile(r"\bConfirmed:\s*(yes|true|confirmed)\b", re.I)
READ_BEFORE_RX = re.compile(r"^Read before:\s*(yes|true)\s*$", re.I | re.M)


def day_or_today(day):
    d = day or dt.date.today().isoformat()
    if not valid_day(d):
        raise Refused("--day %r is no YYYY-MM-DD date" % d)
    return d


def cycle_for_day(day, cycle=None):
    if cycle:
        if not re.fullmatch(schema.CYCLE, cycle):
            raise Refused("--cycle %r is no ISO week (YYYY-Www)" % cycle)
        return cycle
    return dt.date.fromisoformat(day).strftime("%G-W%V")


def records_branch_name(day):
    return "claude/%s/%s-scope-pass" % (common.host_name(), day)


def resolve_scope_one(name, lens_doc=None):
    if lens_doc is None:
        try:
            lens_doc = load_lenses()
        except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
            raise Refused("lenses.json cannot be read (%s)" % e)
    reg, why = registry_or_refusal()
    if why:
        raise Refused(why)
    scopes_reg = reg.get("scopes") or {}
    if name not in scopes_reg:
        raise Refused("no scope %r in the registry" % name)
    raw = scopes_reg[name]
    if not isinstance(raw, dict) or not isinstance(raw.get("repos"), list):
        raise Refused("scope %r in the registry has no list of repos" % name)
    ms = matchers(reg)
    own_fence = fence_for(ms, own=name)
    vpath, vname = vault_info()
    sc = Scope(name, raw, reg.get("repos") or {}, lens_doc, fenced_by=own_fence, vault=vpath)
    return reg, sc, own_fence, vpath, vname, lens_doc


def staging_dir(sc, day):
    """Where drafts sit before `evolve record`: outside `<vault>` and `<layer>` for `atlas`, else `<anchor>`."""
    if sc.vault_records:
        return state_dir() / "staging" / sc.label.replace(":", "-") / day
    return sc.anchor


def deep_lens_for(reg, sc, lens_doc, day):
    d = dt.date.fromisoformat(day)
    serial = (d - dt.timedelta(days=d.weekday())).toordinal() // 7
    usable_names = sorted(k for k, v in (reg.get("scopes") or {}).items() if isinstance(v, dict) and isinstance(v.get("repos"), list))
    idx = usable_names.index(sc.name) if sc.name in usable_names else 0
    na = set(sc.profile.get("not_applicable") or [])
    app = [ln["id"] for ln in lens_doc["lenses"] if ln["id"] not in na] or [ln["id"] for ln in lens_doc["lenses"]]
    return app[(serial + idx) % len(app)]


def research_status(day, now):
    """Check tonight's sextant research artefact: complete within freshness, else `outside: stale`."""
    log = Path(common.LOG_DIR)
    candidates = [log / "sextant" / ("%s-research.json" % day),
                  log / "sextant" / "research" / ("%s.json" % day),
                  log / "sextant" / "research" / ("%s-research.json" % day)]
    rdir = log / "sextant" / "research"
    if rdir.is_dir() and not rdir.is_symlink():
        try:
            candidates += sorted(rdir.glob("*"), key=lambda p: p.stat().st_mtime, reverse=True)[:5]
        except OSError:
            pass
    elif rdir.is_file():
        candidates.append(rdir)
    seen = set()
    for p in candidates:
        rp = str(p)
        if rp in seen or not p.is_file():
            continue
        seen.add(rp)
        try:
            raw = p.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
            mtime = dt.datetime.fromtimestamp(p.stat().st_mtime).astimezone()
        except OSError:
            continue
        age = (now - mtime).total_seconds() / 86400
        if p.suffix == ".json":
            try:
                obj = json.loads(raw)
            except ValueError:
                continue
            if not isinstance(obj, dict):
                continue
            st = obj.get("status")
            if st in ("incomplete", "failed", "stale") or obj.get("complete") is False:
                return {"outside": "stale", "why": "research artefact %s is %s" % (p.name, st or "incomplete")}
            t = parse_time(obj.get("time") or obj.get("date")) or mtime
            if (now - t).total_seconds() / 86400 <= 7:
                return {"outside": "complete", "artefact": p.name}
        elif raw.strip() and age <= 7:
            return {"outside": "complete", "artefact": p.name}
    return {"outside": "stale", "why": "no complete research artefact within 7 days"}


def reconcile_carried(sc, day, own_fence):
    """Read carried `*.findings.json` older than DAY from the scope's records home (or anchor's records/main git)."""
    home = sc.records_home if sc.vault_records else sc.anchor
    by_id = {}
    if home and not own_fence(home):
        edir = home / "evolve"
        try:
            files = sorted(f for f in edir.glob("*.findings.json") if f.name < ("%s.findings.json" % day)) if edir.is_dir() else []
        except OSError:
            files = []
        for f in files:
            try:
                rec = json.load(open(f, encoding="utf-8"))
            except (OSError, ValueError):
                continue
            for fd in (rec.get("findings") if isinstance(rec, dict) and isinstance(rec.get("findings"), list) else []):
                if isinstance(fd, dict) and isinstance(fd.get("id"), str):
                    by_id[fd["id"]] = fd
        if not files and (home / ".git").exists():
            r = git(home, "ls-tree", "--name-only", "HEAD", "evolve/")
            for rel in sorted(r.stdout.splitlines()) if r.returncode == 0 else []:
                if rel.endswith(".findings.json") and os.path.basename(rel) < ("%s.findings.json" % day):
                    sh = git(home, "show", "HEAD:%s" % rel)
                    try:
                        rec = json.loads(sh.stdout) if sh.returncode == 0 else {}
                    except ValueError:
                        rec = {}
                    for fd in (rec.get("findings") if isinstance(rec, dict) and isinstance(rec.get("findings"), list) else []):
                        if isinstance(fd, dict) and isinstance(fd.get("id"), str):
                            by_id[fd["id"]] = fd
    routed, due_checks, cooldowns = [], [], []
    d_cur = dt.date.fromisoformat(day)
    for fid, fd in sorted(by_id.items()):
        st = fd.get("status") if isinstance(fd.get("status"), dict) else {}
        prop, exe, outc = st.get("proposal"), st.get("execution"), st.get("outcome")
        bc = fd.get("benefit_check") if isinstance(fd.get("benefit_check"), dict) else {}
        due = valid_day(bc.get("due"))
        if prop == "routed" and outc not in ("benefit_observed", "closed_verified"):
            routed.append({"id": fid, "execution": exe, "outcome": outc, "due": due})
        if due and due <= day and (prop == "routed" or exe == "shipped") and outc not in ("benefit_observed", "closed_verified"):
            due_checks.append({"id": fid, "due": due, "check": bc.get("check") if not sc.confidential else "due", "outcome": outc})
        cd = fd.get("cooldown")
        fday = valid_day(fd.get("date"))
        if prop in ("parked", "killed") and isinstance(cd, int) and cd > 0 and fday:
            left = cd - (d_cur - dt.date.fromisoformat(fday)).days
            if left > 0:
                cooldowns.append({"id": fid, "proposal": prop, "days_left": left})
    return {"carried_total": len(by_id), "routed": routed, "due_checks": due_checks, "cooldowns": cooldowns}


def _workflow_in_place(repo):
    wf = repo / ".claude" / "workflow.json"
    if not wf.is_file() or (repo / ".claude" / "no-workflow").exists():
        return None, wf
    try:
        w = json.loads(wf.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return set(), wf
    return {str(e).rstrip("/") for e in ((w or {}).get("in_place") or []) if isinstance(e, str)}, wf


def scope_readiness(sc, vpath):
    if sc.profile_error:
        return sc.profile_error
    if not sc.anchor:
        return "scope %s has no anchor (its first repo, named, not a glob)" % sc.label
    if not (sc.anchor / ".git").exists():
        return "its anchor is not cloned here"
    if not vpath or not (vpath / ".git").exists():
        return "atlas's vault is not configured (weekly-run where)"
    if sc.confidential and not (sc.anchor / ".claude" / "words.txt").is_file():
        return "confidential, and its anchor has no .claude/words.txt"
    if sc.vault_records:
        ip, wf = _workflow_in_place(vpath)
        if ip is not None and "evolve" not in ip:
            return "evolve/ is not in the vault's in_place (%s)" % wf
    else:
        ip, wf = _workflow_in_place(sc.anchor)
        if ip is not None:
            missing = [d for d in ("dreams", "evolve") if d not in ip]
            if missing:
                return "%s not in the anchor's in_place (%s)" % (" and ".join(d + "/" for d in missing), wf)
    return None


def write_verb_receipt(sc, cell_id, now):
    p = state_dir() / "receipts" / sc.label.replace(":", "-") / ("%s.json" % cell_id)
    p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = p.with_suffix(".json.tmp")
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps({"time": now.isoformat(timespec="seconds")}) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    os.replace(tmp, p)


def run_collectors(sc, lens_doc, now, record_receipts=True):
    """Run zero-token verb collectors declared in lenses.json or the scope's profile; write receipts on exit 0."""
    col_map = {c["id"]: bool(c.get("required")) for c in lens_doc.get("collectors") or [] if isinstance(c, dict) and c.get("id")}
    req_srcs = {s for c in lens_doc.get("collectors") or [] if c.get("required") for s in c.get("sources") or []}
    ran, errors = [], []
    wd = HERE / "week-digest"
    if wd.is_file():
        try:
            r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(wd), "--days", "7", "--json", "--scope", sc.name],
                               capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=180)
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            r = subprocess.CompletedProcess([], 124, "", "timed out")
        if r.returncode == 0:
            ran.append("week-digest")
            if record_receipts:
                write_verb_receipt(sc, "week-digest", now)
        elif "week-digest" in req_srcs:
            errors.append("collector digest (week-digest): exit %d" % r.returncode)
    else:
        errors.append("collector digest: week-digest missing")
    for idx, src in enumerate(sc.profile.get("sources") or [], 1):
        if src.get("kind") != "verb" or not src.get("collector"):
            continue
        cid = "profile-source-%d" % idx if sc.confidential else src["id"]
        req = col_map.get(src["collector"], False)
        vb = peer(src["name"])
        if not vb:
            if req:
                errors.append("collector %s (%s): verb not installed" % (src["collector"], cid))
            continue
        try:
            r = subprocess.run([str(vb), "--scope", sc.name], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120)
        except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
            r = subprocess.CompletedProcess([], 1, "", "failed")
        if r.returncode == 0:
            ran.append(cid)
            if record_receipts:
                write_verb_receipt(sc, cid, now)
        elif req:
            errors.append("collector %s (%s): exit %d" % (src["collector"], cid, r.returncode))
    return ran, errors


def cmd_where(a):
    day = day_or_today(a.day)
    reg, sc, own_fence, vpath, vname, lens_doc = resolve_scope_one(a.scope)
    now = dt.datetime.now().astimezone()
    why = scope_readiness(sc, vpath)
    stg = staging_dir(sc, day)
    rs = research_status(day, now)
    dl = deep_lens_for(reg, sc, lens_doc, day)
    prof_disp = str(sc.profile_file) if sc.profile_file.exists() and not sc.confidential else ("present" if sc.profile_file.exists() else "none")
    rows = [
        ("scope", sc.name),
        ("label", sc.label),
        ("confidential", "true" if sc.confidential else "false"),
        ("login", common.scope_login(sc.name) or "default"),
        ("anchor", str(sc.anchor or "MISSING")),
        ("records", str(sc.records_home or "MISSING")),
        ("vault-records", "true" if sc.vault_records else "false"),
        ("staging", str(stg or "MISSING")),
        ("profile", prof_disp),
        ("deep-lens", dl),
        ("outside", rs["outside"]),
        ("vault", str(vpath or "MISSING")),
        ("vault-name", vname),
        ("inbox", str(vpath / "inbox" / "upstream" / ("%s.md" % sc.name)) if vpath else "MISSING"),
        ("records-branch", records_branch_name(day)),
        ("ready", "yes" if not why else "no — %s" % why),
    ]
    for k, v in rows:
        print("%s %s" % (k, v))
    return 0 if not why else 1


def _commit_vault_paths(vpath, vname, msg, rels):
    """Commit RELS in the vault through `SCOPE_PASS_COMMIT` (suite stand-in) or atlas's `knowledge-commit`."""
    override = os.environ.get("SCOPE_PASS_COMMIT")
    if override:
        cmd = [*override.split(), vname, "-m", msg, *rels]
    else:
        kc = peer("knowledge-commit")
        if not kc:
            return False, "atlas's knowledge-commit is not installed"
        cmd = [str(kc), vname, "-m", msg, *rels]
    r = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=str(vpath), capture_output=True, text=True)
    return r.returncode == 0, (r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()[-240:]


def _append_vault_log(vpath, scope_name, day, word):
    if not vpath or not vpath.is_dir():
        return False
    log_md = vpath / "log.md"
    prefix = "- %s evolve --scope %s:" % (day, scope_name)
    line = "%s %s" % (prefix, word)
    old = log_md.read_text(encoding="utf-8") if log_md.is_file() else "# Log\n\n"
    lines = [l for l in old.splitlines() if not l.startswith(prefix)]
    lines.append(line)
    log_md.write_text("\n".join(lines) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    return True


def _write_state_receipt(sc, day, rc_obj):
    p = state_dir() / "receipts" / sc.label.replace(":", "-") / ("%s-receipt.json" % day)
    p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    p.write_text(json.dumps(rc_obj, indent=1) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    return p


def cmd_open(a):
    day = day_or_today(a.day)
    cycle = cycle_for_day(day, a.cycle)
    reg, sc, own_fence, vpath, vname, lens_doc = resolve_scope_one(a.scope)
    if sc.profile_error:
        raise Refused("scope %s: %s" % (sc.label, sc.profile_error))
    now = dt.datetime.now().astimezone()
    ran, col_errors = run_collectors(sc, lens_doc, now, record_receipts=True)
    if col_errors:
        raise Refused("collector failed (held, never quiet): " + "; ".join(col_errors))
    rec = reconcile_carried(sc, day, own_fence)
    rs = research_status(day, now)
    dl = deep_lens_for(reg, sc, lens_doc, day)
    base = read_baseline(sc)
    cells, extra = scope_cells(sc, lens_doc, own_fence, now)
    scope_state(sc, own_fence, base, a.session)
    m = manifest(sc, lens_doc, cells, extra, now, None, base)
    if a.session:
        m["pass_session"] = a.session
    label_file(sc, "").parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    for suffix in ("", ".opening"):
        with open(label_file(sc, suffix), "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            json.dump(m, fh, indent=1)
    m_sha = file_sha(label_file(sc, ".opening"))
    why = list(m["why"])
    if rec["due_checks"]:
        why.append("%d benefit check%s due" % (len(rec["due_checks"]), "" if len(rec["due_checks"]) == 1 else "s"))
    quiet_earned = bool(m["quiet_ok"] and not rec["due_checks"])
    pkt = {
        "scope": sc.label, "day": day, "cycle": cycle, "cutoff": m["cutoff"],
        "deep_lens": dl, "outside": rs["outside"], "outside_detail": rs,
        "collectors_ran": ran, "reconciled": rec,
        "quiet_ok": quiet_earned, "why": why, "manifest_sha": m_sha,
        "staging": str(staging_dir(sc, day)) if not sc.confidential else None,
    }
    if a.quiet_exit and quiet_earned:
        rc_obj = {"receipt": "quiet", "scope": sc.label, "cycle": cycle, "day": day,
                  "cutoff": m["cutoff"], "cost_usd": 0.0, "manifest_sha": m_sha,
                  "time": now.isoformat(timespec="seconds")}
        if schema.validate("receipt", rc_obj):
            raise Refused("quiet receipt failed schema validation")
        _write_state_receipt(sc, day, rc_obj)
        if vpath and (vpath / ".git").exists() and not os.environ.get("EVOLVE_NO_COMMIT"):
            if _append_vault_log(vpath, sc.name, day, "quiet"):
                _commit_vault_paths(vpath, vname, "Evolve: %s %s quiet" % (sc.label, day), ["log.md"])
        pkt["receipt"] = rc_obj
        if a.json:
            print(json.dumps(pkt, indent=1))
        else:
            print("evolve open %s: quiet earned at $0 (cutoff %s)" % (sc.label, m["cutoff"]))
        return 3
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps(pkt, indent=1))
    else:
        print("scope %s (%s): deep-lens %s, outside %s, %d carried (%d due check%s), quiet %s" % (
            sc.label, cycle, dl, rs["outside"], rec["carried_total"], len(rec["due_checks"]),
            "" if len(rec["due_checks"]) == 1 else "s", "earned" if quiet_earned else "not allowed — " + "; ".join(why)))
    return 0


def _deterministic_finding_checks(rec, sc, lens_doc):
    """Cold-artefact deterministic checks beyond field types: outcome_classes, lenses, blind-spot sensors, strength n."""
    base_classes = dict(lens_doc.get("outcome_classes") or {})
    if sc is not None and not sc.profile_error and isinstance(sc.profile.get("outcome_classes"), dict):
        base_classes.update(sc.profile["outcome_classes"])
    elif isinstance(rec, dict) and rec.get("scope"):
        base_classes = _classes_for_scope(rec.get("scope"), base_classes, lens_doc, explicit=False)
    probs = list(schema.validate("findings", rec, base_classes))
    lens_ids = set(lens_doc.get("_lens_ids") or [])
    na = set((sc.profile.get("not_applicable") if sc and not sc.profile_error else None) or [])
    fs = rec.get("findings") if isinstance(rec, dict) and isinstance(rec.get("findings"), list) else []
    seen_ids = set()
    for i, f in enumerate(fs):
        if not isinstance(f, dict):
            continue
        fid = f.get("id")
        if isinstance(fid, str):
            if fid in seen_ids:
                probs.append("findings[%d].id: duplicate id %r in findings file" % (i, fid))
            seen_ids.add(fid)
        ln = f.get("lens")
        if isinstance(ln, str) and ln:
            if ln not in lens_ids:
                probs.append("findings[%d].lens: %r is no lens lenses.json declares" % (i, ln))
            elif ln in na:
                probs.append("findings[%d].lens: %r is marked not_applicable in the scope profile" % (i, ln))
        ac = (f.get("acceptance_check") or "").strip() if isinstance(f.get("acceptance_check"), str) else ""
        if ac.lower() in TRIVIAL_CHECK:
            probs.append("findings[%d].acceptance_check: %r is no runnable check" % (i, f.get("acceptance_check")))
        if f.get("kind") == "blind_spot":
            combined = "%s %s" % (f.get("intervention") or "", ac)
            if not SENSOR_RX.search(combined):
                probs.append("findings[%d].intervention: a blind_spot candidate must add a sensor or scheduled observation" % i)
        if f.get("kind") == "strength" and f.get("proposed_route") not in (None, "park"):
            refs = f.get("evidence_refs") if isinstance(f.get("evidence_refs"), list) else []
            max_n = max([r.get("count", 0) for r in refs if isinstance(r, dict) and isinstance(r.get("count"), int)] or [0])
            if max_n < 5:
                probs.append("findings[%d]: a strength with n < 5 (%d) is a watch line (park), not %r" % (i, max_n, f.get("proposed_route")))
        if f.get("proposed_route") in ("build", "sound", "pin"):
            ce = f.get("counterevidence")
            if not isinstance(ce, str) or len(ce.strip()) < 3:
                probs.append("findings[%d].counterevidence: required on a %s proposal" % (i, f.get("proposed_route")))
    return probs


CRITIC_PROMPT = (
    "You are a cold, blinded critic reviewing a scope pass's candidate findings artefact. You have NOT been told "
    "the owner's preferences or past overrules. Judge each finding strictly on the artefact before you: "
    "(1) does `acceptance_check` test what `intervention` changes, and is `benefit_check` falsifiable on its due date? "
    "(2) does `observation` follow from `evidence_counts`, and was `counterevidence` genuinely weighed? "
    "(3) if `kind` is `blind_spot`, does `intervention` add a real sensor or scheduled observation rather than prose? "
    "Return JSON matching the schema: for each finding id, `verdict` (`pass` or `drop`) and `reason` (one short sentence).")


def _load_gate_mod():
    gpath = HERE.parent.parent / "regatta" / "bin" / "gate"
    if not gpath.is_file():
        return None
    from importlib.machinery import SourceFileLoader
    return SourceFileLoader("gate", str(gpath)).load_module()


def _run_blinded_critic(rec, sc, require_model=False):
    """Run the gate's `evolve.critic` row over a stripped cold packet; return (issues, meta)."""
    fs = [f for f in (rec.get("findings") or []) if isinstance(f, dict) and isinstance(f.get("id"), str)]
    if not fs:
        return [], {"gate": "no_findings", "cost_usd": 0.0}
    gate_mod = _load_gate_mod()
    if gate_mod is None:
        if require_model:
            raise Refused("gate module is missing")
        return [], {"gate": "skipped", "why": "no gate module", "cost_usd": 0.0}
    try:
        row = gate_mod.resolve(CRITIC_SITE)
    except Exception as e:   # noqa: BLE001
        if type(e).__name__ == "GateOff":
            raise Refused("%s is off with when_off=fail" % CRITIC_SITE)
        raise Refused("%s: %s" % (CRITIC_SITE, str(e).splitlines()[0][:160]))
    if row is None:
        return [], {"gate": "skipped", "why": "off", "cost_usd": 0.0}
    if row.get("provider") != "claude":
        if sc is not None and sc.confidential:
            raise Refused("%s: provider %r refused on confidential scope (Anthropic-only)" % (CRITIC_SITE, row.get("provider")))
        try:
            guarded = set(gate_mod._jev_module().GUARDED)
            if sc is not None and any(m.name in guarded or str(m) in guarded for m in sc.members):
                raise Refused("%s: provider %r refused on guarded scope" % (CRITIC_SITE, row.get("provider")))
        except Refused:
            raise
        except Exception:   # noqa: BLE001
            raise Refused("%s: guard list unreadable for provider %r" % (CRITIC_SITE, row.get("provider")))
    cold = []
    for f in fs:
        refs = [{"source": ("source-%d" % (j + 1) if sc and sc.confidential else r.get("source")), "count": r.get("count")}
                for j, r in enumerate(f.get("evidence_refs") or []) if isinstance(r, dict)]
        cold.append({
            "id": f["id"], "kind": f.get("kind"), "lens": f.get("lens"),
            "observation": f.get("observation"), "hypothesis": f.get("hypothesis"),
            "counterevidence": f.get("counterevidence"), "intervention": f.get("intervention"),
            "smallest_test": f.get("smallest_test"), "acceptance_check": f.get("acceptance_check"),
            "benefit_check": f.get("benefit_check"), "proposed_route": f.get("proposed_route"),
            "evidence_counts": refs,
        })
    ids = [c["id"] for c in cold]
    item_schema = {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": False, "required": ["verdict", "reason"],
                   "properties": {"verdict": {"type": "string", "enum": ["pass", "drop"]},
                                  "reason": {"type": "string"}}}
    jschema = {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": False, "required": ids,
               "properties": {fid: item_schema for fid in ids}}
    prompt = CRITIC_PROMPT + "\n\nFindings artefact:\n" + json.dumps(cold, indent=1)
    cbin = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_BIN") or shutil.which("claude")
    if not cbin:
        if require_model:
            raise Refused("%s: claude binary not found" % CRITIC_SITE)
        return [], {"gate": "skipped", "why": "claude not installed", "cost_usd": 0.0}
    cmd = [cbin, "-p", *gate_mod.claude_flags(row), "--output-format", "json",
           "--tools", "", "--setting-sources", "", "--no-session-persistence", "--json-schema", json.dumps(jschema)]
    try:
        p = subprocess.run(cmd, input=prompt, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=300,
                           env={k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k != "CLAUDECODE"})
        res = json.loads(p.stdout)
        got = res.get("structured_output")
        if not isinstance(got, dict):
            got = json.loads(res.get("result") or "")
        cost = float(res.get("total_cost_usd") or 0.0)
        if res.get("is_error") or not isinstance(got, dict):
            raise ValueError("bad critic reply")
    except (OSError, ValueError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
        if require_model:
            raise Refused("%s failed: %s" % (CRITIC_SITE, type(e).__name__))
        return [], {"gate": "skipped", "why": "call failed (%s)" % type(e).__name__, "cost_usd": 0.0}
    issues = []
    for fid in ids:
        v = got.get(fid) if isinstance(got.get(fid), dict) else {}
        if v.get("verdict") == "drop":
            issues.append("critic (%s): %s" % (fid, str(v.get("reason") or "dropped by blinded critic")[:200]))
    return issues, {"gate": "ran", "model": row.get("model"), "cost_usd": cost, "verdicts": got}


def cmd_critic(a):
    try:
        lens_doc = load_lenses()
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        raise Refused("lenses.json cannot be read (%s)" % e)
    try:
        with open(a.file, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            rec = json.load(fh)
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        raise Refused("findings file cannot be read (%s)" % type(e).__name__)
    sc = None
    if a.scope:
        _, sc, _, _, _, _ = resolve_scope_one(a.scope, lens_doc)
        if sc.profile_error:
            raise Refused("scope %s: %s" % (sc.label, sc.profile_error))
    det = _deterministic_finding_checks(rec, sc, lens_doc)
    mod_issues, meta = _run_blinded_critic(rec, sc, require_model=a.require_model)
    all_issues = det + mod_issues
    out = {"ok": not all_issues, "deterministic": det, "critic": mod_issues, "meta": meta}
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps(out, indent=1))
    else:
        for msg in all_issues:
            print("  FAIL %s" % msg)
        print("critic: %s (%s)" % ("clean" if not all_issues else "%d issue%s" % (len(all_issues), "" if len(all_issues) == 1 else "s"),
                                   meta.get("gate")))
    return 0 if not all_issues else 1


def _plumb_commit_repo(repo, br, main_name, msg, rels):
    """Commit RELS (present in REPO) onto refs/heads/BR using a private GIT_INDEX_FILE; remove untracked copies."""
    here = [r for r in rels if (repo / r).is_file()]
    if not here:
        return True, ""
    ref = "refs/heads/%s" % br
    old = git(repo, "rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", ref + "^{commit}").stdout.strip()
    base = old
    if not base:
        for cand in ("refs/remotes/origin/%s" % main_name, "refs/heads/%s" % main_name, "HEAD"):
            tip = git(repo, "rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", cand + "^{commit}").stdout.strip()
            if tip:
                base = tip
                break
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="evolve-rec-") as tmp:
        env = {**os.environ, "GIT_INDEX_FILE": str(Path(tmp) / "index"), "GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT": "0"}

        def g(*args):
            return subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(repo), *args], capture_output=True, text=True, env=env)
        s0 = g("read-tree", base) if base else g("read-tree", "--empty")
        if s0.returncode != 0:
            return False, (s0.stderr or s0.stdout).strip()
        for r in here:
            h = g("hash-object", "-w", "--", r)
            if h.returncode != 0:
                return False, (h.stderr or h.stdout).strip()
            u = g("update-index", "--add", "--cacheinfo", "100644,%s,%s" % (h.stdout.strip(), r))
            if u.returncode != 0:
                return False, (u.stderr or u.stdout).strip()
        tr = g("write-tree")
        if tr.returncode != 0:
            return False, (tr.stderr or tr.stdout).strip()
        tree = tr.stdout.strip()
        if not base or git(repo, "rev-parse", base + "^{tree}").stdout.strip() != tree:
            c = g("commit-tree", tree, *(["-p", base] if base else []), "-m", msg)
            if c.returncode != 0:
                return False, (c.stderr or c.stdout).strip()
            up = g("update-ref", ref, c.stdout.strip(), *([old] if old else []))
            if up.returncode != 0:
                return False, (up.stderr or up.stdout).strip()
    for r in here:
        if git(repo, "ls-files", "--error-unmatch", "--", r).returncode != 0:
            try:
                (repo / r).unlink()
            except OSError:
                pass
    if git(repo, "remote", "get-url", "origin").returncode == 0:
        p = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(repo), "push", "-q", "origin", "+%s:%s" % (ref, ref)],
                           capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120, env={**os.environ, "GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT": "0"})
        if p.returncode != 0:
            return False, "push failed: %s" % (p.stderr or p.stdout).strip()[-200:]
        pr_cmd = os.environ.get("SCOPE_PASS_PR")
        if pr_cmd:
            subprocess.run([*pr_cmd.split(), "open", str(repo), br, main_name], capture_output=True, text=True)
    return True, ""


def _export_open_findings(sc, day, findings_list):
    """Write an open scope's finding objects to `$ASKS_FINDINGS/<scope>-<day>.json` for plumb's `asks` matcher."""
    if sc.confidential:
        return None
    fdir = Path(os.environ.get("ASKS_FINDINGS") or (Path(common.LOG_DIR) / "evolve" / "findings"))
    fdir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    out = fdir / ("%s-%s.json" % (sc.name, day))
    tmp = out.with_suffix(".json.tmp")
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(findings_list, indent=1) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    os.replace(tmp, out)
    return out


def _promote_scope_baseline(sc, session=None):
    src = label_file(sc, ".opening")
    if not src.is_file():
        return False
    try:
        m = json.loads(src.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        if schema.validate("manifest", m):
            return False
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return False
    if session:
        m["pass_session"] = session
    label_file(sc, ".complete").write_text(json.dumps(m, indent=1) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    return True


def cmd_record(a):
    day = day_or_today(a.day)
    cycle = cycle_for_day(day, a.cycle)
    _, sc, own_fence, vpath, vname, lens_doc = resolve_scope_one(a.scope)
    if sc.profile_error:
        raise Refused("scope %s: %s" % (sc.label, sc.profile_error))
    now = dt.datetime.now().astimezone()
    open_m_file = label_file(sc, ".opening")
    if not open_m_file.is_file():
        base = read_baseline(sc)
        cells, extra = scope_cells(sc, lens_doc, own_fence, now)
        scope_state(sc, own_fence, base, a.session)
        m = manifest(sc, lens_doc, cells, extra, now, None, base)
        if a.session:
            m["pass_session"] = a.session
        open_m_file.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        open_m_file.write_text(json.dumps(m, indent=1) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    else:
        m = json.loads(open_m_file.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    m_sha = file_sha(open_m_file)
    if a.quiet:
        rec_c = reconcile_carried(sc, day, own_fence)
        if not m.get("quiet_ok") or rec_c["due_checks"]:
            reasons = list(m.get("why") or []) + (["benefit check due"] if rec_c["due_checks"] else [])
            print("%s record: quiet refused for %s — %s" % (PROG, sc.label, "; ".join(reasons) or "not earned"), file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        rc_obj = {"receipt": "quiet", "scope": sc.label, "cycle": cycle, "day": day,
                  "cutoff": m.get("cutoff"), "cost_usd": 0.0, "manifest_sha": m_sha,
                  "time": now.isoformat(timespec="seconds")}
        if schema.validate("receipt", rc_obj):
            print("%s record: quiet receipt failed schema check" % PROG, file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        _write_state_receipt(sc, day, rc_obj)
        if vpath and (vpath / ".git").exists():
            _append_vault_log(vpath, sc.name, day, "quiet")
            ok, err = _commit_vault_paths(vpath, vname, "Evolve: %s %s quiet" % (sc.label, day), ["log.md"])
            if not ok:
                print("%s record: vault log commit failed — %s" % (PROG, err), file=sys.stderr)
                return 1
        print("evolve record %s: quiet (%s)" % (sc.label, day))
        return 0

    stg = staging_dir(sc, day)
    f_json = (stg / "evolve" / ("%s.findings.json" % day)) if stg else None
    f_md = (stg / "evolve" / ("%s.md" % day)) if stg else None
    if (not f_json or not f_json.is_file()) and sc.records_home:
        alt_j = sc.records_home / "evolve" / ("%s.findings.json" % day)
        alt_m = sc.records_home / "evolve" / ("%s.md" % day)
        if alt_j.is_file():
            f_json, f_md = alt_j, alt_m
    if not f_json or not f_json.is_file() or not f_md or not f_md.is_file():
        print("%s record: missing drafted evolve/%s.findings.json or evolve/%s.md in %s" % (PROG, day, day, stg), file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    try:
        findings_obj = json.loads(f_json.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        md_text = f_md.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        print("%s record: unreadable findings or markdown (%s)" % (PROG, type(e).__name__), file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    if not md_text.strip():
        print("%s record: evolve/%s.md is empty" % (PROG, day), file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    expected_scopes = {sc.name, sc.label}
    if findings_obj.get("scope") not in expected_scopes:
        print("%s record: findings scope %r does not match %s" % (PROG, findings_obj.get("scope"), sc.label), file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    probs = _deterministic_finding_checks(findings_obj, sc, lens_doc)
    if probs:
        for p in probs:
            print("%s record: %s" % (PROG, p), file=sys.stderr)
        return 1

    br = records_branch_name(day)
    if sc.vault_records:
        if not vpath or not (vpath / ".git").exists():
            print("%s record: atlas's vault is not configured" % PROG, file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        rc_obj = {"receipt": "complete", "scope": sc.label, "cycle": cycle, "day": day,
                  "cutoff": findings_obj.get("cutoff") or m.get("cutoff"),
                  "cost_usd": a.cost, "records_ref": "main", "manifest_sha": m_sha,
                  "time": now.isoformat(timespec="seconds")}
        if schema.validate("receipt", rc_obj):
            print("%s record: receipt failed schema check" % PROG, file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        ve = vpath / "evolve"
        ve.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        rels = ["evolve/%s.findings.json" % day, "evolve/%s.md" % day, "evolve/%s-receipt.json" % day]
        (vpath / rels[0]).write_text(json.dumps(findings_obj, indent=1) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
        (vpath / rels[1]).write_text(md_text, encoding="utf-8")
        (vpath / rels[2]).write_text(json.dumps(rc_obj, indent=1) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
        _append_vault_log(vpath, sc.name, day, "complete")
        ip, _ = _workflow_in_place(vpath)
        if ip is not None and "evolve" not in ip:
            rc_obj["records_ref"] = br
            (vpath / rels[2]).write_text(json.dumps(rc_obj, indent=1) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
            ok_b, err_b = _plumb_commit_repo(vpath, br, "main", "Evolve: %s %s" % (sc.label, day), rels)
            ok_l, err_l = _commit_vault_paths(vpath, vname, "Evolve: %s %s log" % (sc.label, day), ["log.md"])
            if not (ok_b and ok_l):
                print("%s record: vault commit failed — %s" % (PROG, err_b or err_l), file=sys.stderr)
                return 1
        else:
            ok, err = _commit_vault_paths(vpath, vname, "Evolve: %s %s" % (sc.label, day), rels + ["log.md"])
            if not ok:
                print("%s record: vault commit failed — %s" % (PROG, err), file=sys.stderr)
                return 1
        if stg and stg != vpath:
            shutil.rmtree(stg, ignore_errors=True)
    else:
        if not sc.anchor or not (sc.anchor / ".git").exists():
            print("%s record: scope %s has no cloned anchor" % (PROG, sc.label), file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        has_dream = (sc.anchor / "dreams" / ("%s.md" % day)).is_file() or (sc.anchor / "dreams" / ("%s-upstream.md" % day)).is_file()
        sp_rc_obj = {}
        if sc.confidential and not has_dream:
            sp_chk = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(HERE / "scope-pass"), "receipt", sc.name, "--day", day],
                                    capture_output=True, text=True)
            if sp_chk.returncode != 0:
                print("%s record: confidential scope requires dreams/%s.md and dreams/%s-upstream.md for export gate" % (PROG, day, day), file=sys.stderr)
                return 1
            try:
                sp_rc_obj = json.loads(sp_chk.stdout)
            except ValueError:
                sp_rc_obj = {}
        elif has_dream:
            sp = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(HERE / "scope-pass"), "record", sc.name, "--day", day, "--cycle", cycle],
                                capture_output=True, text=True)
            if sp.stdout:
                sys.stdout.write(sp.stdout)
            if sp.stderr:
                sys.stderr.write(sp.stderr)
            if sp.returncode != 0:
                return sp.returncode
            sp_r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(HERE / "scope-pass"), "receipt", sc.name, "--day", day],
                                  capture_output=True, text=True)
            if sp_r.returncode == 0:
                try:
                    sp_rc_obj = json.loads(sp_r.stdout)
                except ValueError:
                    sp_rc_obj = {}
        rc_obj = {
            "receipt": "complete", "scope": sc.label, "cycle": cycle, "day": day,
            "cutoff": findings_obj.get("cutoff") or m.get("cutoff"),
            "cost_usd": a.cost if a.cost is not None else sp_rc_obj.get("cost_usd"),
            "records_ref": br, "sha256": sp_rc_obj.get("sha256"), "judge_rev": sp_rc_obj.get("judge_rev"),
            "manifest_sha": m_sha, "time": now.isoformat(timespec="seconds"),
        }
        if schema.validate("receipt", rc_obj):
            print("%s record: receipt failed schema check" % PROG, file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        ae = sc.anchor / "evolve"
        ae.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        rels = ["evolve/%s.findings.json" % day, "evolve/%s.md" % day, "evolve/%s-receipt.json" % day]
        if f_json.resolve() != (sc.anchor / rels[0]).resolve():
            (sc.anchor / rels[0]).write_text(json.dumps(findings_obj, indent=1) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
        if f_md.resolve() != (sc.anchor / rels[1]).resolve():
            (sc.anchor / rels[1]).write_text(md_text, encoding="utf-8")
        (sc.anchor / rels[2]).write_text(json.dumps(rc_obj, indent=1) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
        wf_file = sc.anchor / ".claude" / "workflow.json"
        main_name = "main"
        if wf_file.is_file():
            try:
                main_name = json.loads(wf_file.read_text(encoding="utf-8")).get("main") or "main"
            except (OSError, ValueError):
                pass
        ok, err = _plumb_commit_repo(sc.anchor, br, main_name, "Evolve: %s %s" % (sc.label, day), rels)
        if not ok:
            print("%s record: records branch commit failed — %s" % (PROG, err), file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        if not has_dream and vpath and (vpath / ".git").exists():
            _append_vault_log(vpath, sc.name, day, "complete")
            ok_v, err_v = _commit_vault_paths(vpath, vname, "Evolve: %s %s" % (sc.label, day), ["log.md"])
            if not ok_v:
                print("%s record: vault log commit failed — %s" % (PROG, err_v), file=sys.stderr)
                return 1

    _write_state_receipt(sc, day, rc_obj)
    _export_open_findings(sc, day, findings_obj["findings"])
    _promote_scope_baseline(sc, session=a.session)
    print("evolve record %s: complete (%d finding%s)" % (
        sc.label, len(findings_obj["findings"]), "" if len(findings_obj["findings"]) == 1 else "s"))
    return 0


def _inspect_meetings_dir(mdir, repo_root=None):
    """Inspect repo-committed `.md` meeting notes in MDIR; never read uncommitted drafts or recordings."""
    if not mdir or not mdir.is_dir():
        return {"state": "source_missing", "meetings": 0, "prebriefs_read": 0, "commitments": 0,
                "undated_commitments": 0, "unconfirmed_commitments": 0, "uncommitted_ignored": 0, "recordings_refused": 0,
                "summary": "no committed meeting notes"}
    root = repo_root
    if root is None:
        r = git(mdir, "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel")
        root = Path(r.stdout.strip()) if r.returncode == 0 and r.stdout.strip() else None
    tracked = set()
    if root is not None:
        ls = git(root, "ls-files", "--", str(mdir))
        for rel in ls.stdout.splitlines() if ls.returncode == 0 else []:
            tracked.add(os.path.realpath(root / rel))
    meetings = prebriefs_read = commitments = undated = unconfirmed = uncommitted = recordings = 0
    for f in sorted(mdir.iterdir()):
        if f.is_symlink() or not f.is_file():
            continue
        if f.suffix.lower() in RECORDING_EXTS:
            recordings += 1
            continue
        if f.suffix.lower() != ".md" or f.name.lower() == "readme.md":
            continue
        if root is not None and os.path.realpath(f) not in tracked:
            uncommitted += 1
            continue   # read-only until committed by the owner
        try:
            txt = f.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
        except OSError:
            continue
        meetings += 1
        if READ_BEFORE_RX.search(txt):
            prebriefs_read += 1
        in_comm = False
        for raw_line in txt.splitlines():
            s = raw_line.strip()
            if s.startswith("<!--") or s.endswith("-->"):
                continue
            if s.startswith("## "):
                in_comm = s.lower().startswith("## commitment")
                continue
            if in_comm and IF_THEN_RX.match(raw_line):
                if "<condition" in s and "<YYYY-MM-DD>" in s:
                    continue   # unedited template placeholder
                commitments += 1
                dm = DUE_RX.search(s)
                if not dm or not valid_day(dm.group(1)):
                    undated += 1
                if not CONFIRMED_RX.search(s):
                    unconfirmed += 1
    if meetings == 0:
        return {"state": "source_missing", "meetings": 0, "prebriefs_read": 0, "commitments": 0,
                "undated_commitments": 0, "unconfirmed_commitments": 0, "uncommitted_ignored": uncommitted,
                "recordings_refused": recordings, "summary": "0 committed meetings (%d uncommitted draft%s ignored)" % (
                    uncommitted, "" if uncommitted == 1 else "s")}
    summary = "%d meeting%s, %d pre-brief%s read before; %d commitment%s (%d with no date, %d unconfirmed)" % (
        meetings, "" if meetings == 1 else "s", prebriefs_read, "" if prebriefs_read == 1 else "s",
        commitments, "" if commitments == 1 else "s", undated, unconfirmed)
    return {"state": "observed", "meetings": meetings, "prebriefs_read": prebriefs_read,
            "commitments": commitments, "undated_commitments": undated, "unconfirmed_commitments": unconfirmed,
            "uncommitted_ignored": uncommitted, "recordings_refused": recordings, "summary": summary}


def cmd_meetings(a):
    mdir, root = None, None
    if a.scope:
        _, sc, own_fence, _, _, _ = resolve_scope_one(a.scope)
        cand = sc.anchor / "meetings" if sc.anchor else None
        if sc.vault_records and sc.records_home and (not cand or not cand.exists()) and (sc.records_home / "meetings").exists():
            cand, root = sc.records_home / "meetings", sc.records_home
        else:
            root = sc.anchor
        if cand and own_fence(cand):
            raise Refused("meetings path is fenced")
        mdir = cand
    elif a.path:
        mdir = Path(a.path).expanduser()
    else:
        raise Refused("give a directory path or --scope <scope>")
    res = _inspect_meetings_dir(mdir, repo_root=root)
    ok = res["state"] == "observed" and res["prebriefs_read"] == res["meetings"] and res["undated_commitments"] == 0 and res["recordings_refused"] == 0
    res["ok"] = ok
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps(res, indent=1))
    else:
        print("meetings: %s" % res["summary"])
    return 0 if ok else 1


def _words_of(s):
    return {w for w in re.findall(r"[a-z0-9]{3,}", (s or "").lower()) if w not in {"the", "and", "for", "with", "that", "this", "from", "into", "when", "none", "pass"}}


def cmd_replay(a):
    cutoff = day_or_today(a.cutoff)
    c_date = dt.date.fromisoformat(cutoff)
    end_date = (c_date + dt.timedelta(days=a.window)).isoformat()
    cutoff_end = dt.datetime.fromisoformat(cutoff + "T23:59:59+00:00")
    asks_path = Path(a.asks).expanduser() if a.asks else (Path(common.LOG_DIR) / "plumb" / "asks" / "asks.jsonl")
    f_arg = Path(a.findings).expanduser() if a.findings else Path(os.environ.get("ASKS_FINDINGS") or (Path(common.LOG_DIR) / "evolve" / "findings"))
    asks = []
    if asks_path.is_file():
        for line in asks_path.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines():
            if line.strip():
                try:
                    asks.append(json.loads(line))
                except ValueError:
                    continue
    f_files = [f_arg] if f_arg.is_file() else (sorted(f_arg.glob("*.json")) if f_arg.is_dir() else [])
    single_file = f_arg.is_file()
    findings, masked_future, leaks = [], 0, []
    for fp in f_files:
        try:
            raw = json.loads(fp.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
        items = raw.get("findings") if isinstance(raw, dict) and isinstance(raw.get("findings"), list) else (raw if isinstance(raw, list) else [raw])
        for fd in items:
            if not isinstance(fd, dict) or not fd.get("id"):
                continue
            fday = valid_day(fd.get("date"))
            if fday and fday > cutoff:
                if single_file or a.strict_cutoff:
                    leaks.append("finding %s dated %s after cutoff %s" % (fd["id"], fday, cutoff))
                else:
                    masked_future += 1
                continue
            for ref in fd.get("evidence_refs") or []:
                if isinstance(ref, dict) and ref.get("time"):
                    rt = parse_time(ref["time"])
                    if rt is not None and rt.astimezone(dt.timezone.utc) > cutoff_end:
                        leaks.append("finding %s cites post-cutoff evidence (%s)" % (fd["id"], ref["time"]))
            findings.append(fd)
    by_id = {f["id"]: f for f in findings}
    past_asks = [r for r in asks if isinstance(r, dict) and (valid_day(r.get("date")) or "") <= cutoff]
    future_asks = [r for r in asks if isinstance(r, dict) and cutoff < (valid_day(r.get("date")) or "") <= end_date
                   and (r.get("target") in ("system", "question") or r.get("sieve") == "ask")]
    e_total = e_hit = n_backlog = j_excl = 0
    leads, matched_rows = [], []
    for r in future_asks:
        det = r.get("detect") or "E"
        if det == "J":
            j_excl += 1
            continue
        if det == "N":
            n_backlog += 1
            continue
        e_total += 1
        m = r.get("match") if isinstance(r.get("match"), dict) else {}
        hit = by_id.get(m.get("finding")) if m.get("label") == "anticipated" and m.get("finding") in by_id else None
        if hit is None and r.get("theme"):
            hit = next((f for f in findings if f.get("theme_id") == r.get("theme")), None)
        if hit is None:
            rw = _words_of("%s %s" % (r.get("theme") or "", r.get("text") or ""))
            if rw:
                hit = next((f for f in findings if len(rw & _words_of("%s %s %s" % (f.get("id") or "", f.get("need") or "", f.get("theme_id") or ""))) >= 2), None)
        if hit is not None:
            e_hit += 1
            fday = valid_day(hit.get("date")) or cutoff
            lead = (dt.date.fromisoformat(fday) - dt.date.fromisoformat(r["date"])).days
            leads.append(lead)
            matched_rows.append({"ask": r.get("id"), "finding": hit["id"], "lead_days": lead})
    recall = round(e_hit / e_total, 4) if e_total else None
    out = {
        "cutoff": cutoff, "window_days": a.window, "canary_leak": bool(leaks), "leaks": leaks,
        "past_asks_visible": len(past_asks), "findings_at_cutoff": len(findings), "masked_future_findings": masked_future,
        "future_e_asks": e_total, "anticipated_e": e_hit, "recall_e": recall,
        "backlog_n": n_backlog, "excluded_j": j_excl,
        "median_lead_days": sorted(leads)[len(leads) // 2] if leads else None,
        "matches": matched_rows,
    }
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps(out, indent=1))
    else:
        if leaks:
            for lk in leaks:
                print("  LEAK %s" % lk)
        print("replay @ %s (+%dd): %d/%d E anticipated (recall %s), %d N backlog, %d J outside, canary_leak=%s" % (
            cutoff, a.window, e_hit, e_total, "n/a" if recall is None else "%.2f" % recall, n_backlog, j_excl, bool(leaks)))
    return 1 if leaks else 0


def _shadow_findings(sc, lens_doc, cells, rec_carried, meetings_res, day, cycle, cutoff):
    """Synthesise up to 5 schema-valid shadow findings from real coverage cells, bars and meetings."""
    out = []
    due_day = (dt.date.fromisoformat(day) + dt.timedelta(days=28)).isoformat()
    bars = (sc.profile.get("bars") if isinstance(sc.profile.get("bars"), dict) else {}) if not sc.profile_error else {}
    na = set(sc.profile.get("not_applicable") or []) if not sc.profile_error else set()
    oc_map = dict(lens_doc.get("outcome_classes") or {})
    if not sc.profile_error and isinstance(sc.profile.get("outcome_classes"), dict):
        oc_map.update(sc.profile["outcome_classes"])
    default_oc = "code" if "code" in oc_map else next(iter(oc_map))
    noncode_oc = next((k for k in (sc.profile.get("outcome_classes") or {})), None) or (
        "approved_cut" if sc.name == "film" and "approved_cut" in oc_map else default_oc)
    lvl_of = {ln["id"]: (ln.get("levels") or ["PW"])[0] for ln in lens_doc["lenses"]}

    def mk(fid_slug, kind, lens_id, need, obs, interv, check_cmd, source_id, count, route="propose", oc=None):
        fid = re.sub(r"[^a-z0-9._-]", "-", ("%s-%s" % (sc.label.replace(":", "-"), fid_slug)).lower())[:72].strip("-")
        use_oc = oc or (noncode_oc if lens_id in ("strategy", "product") and sc.name not in ("regatta", "atlas") else default_oc)
        obs_win = int((oc_map.get(use_oc) or {}).get("observation_days", 28))
        b_due = (dt.date.fromisoformat(day) + dt.timedelta(days=max(7, obs_win))).isoformat()
        f = {
            "id": fid, "theme_id": fid_slug, "scope": sc.label, "cycle": cycle, "date": day,
            "need": need, "process_revision": "evolve-scope@s5",
            "kind": kind, "level": lvl_of.get(lens_id, "PW"), "lens": lens_id, "goal_ref": None,
            "evidence_refs": [{"source": source_id, "count": int(count)}],
            "source_freshness": {source_id: 0.0},
            "observation": obs, "hypothesis": "unknown",
            "counterevidence": "Source may be intentionally idle in a quiet week; check next cycle before widening.",
            "p_success": 0.7, "intervention": interv, "alternatives": ["park until next cycle"],
            "smallest_test": check_cmd, "acceptance_check": check_cmd,
            "benefit_check": {"check": "cell %s reads observed on %s" % (source_id, sc.label), "due": b_due if valid_day(b_due) else due_day},
            "observation_window": obs_win, "outcome_class": use_oc,
            "reversible": True, "auto_constructible": route == "build", "auto_activatable": False,
            "size": "xs", "est_list_usd": 2.0, "owner_minutes": 2, "maintenance_cost": None,
            "proposed_route": route, "privacy_class": "confidential" if sc.confidential else "open",
            "cooldown": 14, "prior_ids": [], "supersedes": None,
            "found_by": "pass", "also_found_by": [],
            "status": {"proposal": "proposed", "execution": None, "outcome": None},
            "action_version": 1, "target_scope": sc.label,
        }
        f["action_id"] = schema.action_id(f["id"], 1, sc.label)
        return f

    if "strategy" not in na:
        ns_cell = next((c for c in cells if c["source"] == "north-star"), None)
        pr_cell = next((c for c in cells if c["source"] == "principles"), None)
        if "strategy" not in bars and (not ns_cell or ns_cell["state"] != "observed") and (not pr_cell or pr_cell["state"] != "observed"):
            out.append(mk("strategy-no-bar", "gap", "strategy", "declare a measurable strategy bar for the scope",
                          "no bar for this lens: neither north-star.json nor PRINCIPLES.md declares a target for %s" % sc.label,
                          "Declare `bars.strategy` in aurora/scopes/%s.json or add PRINCIPLES.md" % sc.label,
                          "evolve coverage --scope %s --json shows north-star or principles observed" % sc.name,
                          "principles", 0, route="propose"))
    if "meetings" not in na and meetings_res["state"] == "observed" and (meetings_res["prebriefs_read"] < meetings_res["meetings"] or meetings_res["undated_commitments"] > 0):
        out.append(mk("meetings-cadence", "gap", "meetings", "pre-briefs read before and dated if-then commitments",
                      meetings_res["summary"],
                      "Use templates/meeting.md with `Read before: yes` and dated `due: YYYY-MM-DD` commitments",
                      "evolve meetings --scope %s exits 0" % sc.name,
                      "meeting-notes", meetings_res["meetings"], route="propose"))
    for c in cells:
        if len(out) >= 5:
            break
        if c["state"] in ("unread", "inaccessible", "stale") or c.get("overdue"):
            src = c["source"]
            out.append(mk("blind-%s" % src, "blind_spot", c["lens"],
                          "restore fresh observation on %s/%s" % (c["lens"], src),
                          "coverage cell %s/%s is %s (%s)" % (c["lens"], src, c["state"], c.get("why") or "unseen"),
                          "Add a scheduled collector sensor or refresh %s in %s's coverage register" % (src, sc.label),
                          "evolve coverage --scope %s --json marks %s observed" % (sc.name, src),
                          src, 1, route="propose"))
    for c in cells:
        if len(out) >= 5:
            break
        if c["state"] == "source_missing" and c["lens"] not in na:
            src = c["source"]
            out.append(mk("missing-%s" % src, "blind_spot", c["lens"],
                          "wire sensor or exclude %s/%s with review date" % (c["lens"], src),
                          "coverage cell %s/%s is source_missing" % (c["lens"], src),
                          "Wire collector log for %s or declare a dated exclusion in aurora/scopes/%s.json" % (src, sc.label),
                          "evolve coverage --scope %s --json has %s observed or excluded" % (sc.name, src),
                          src, 0, route="propose"))
    return {"version": 1, "scope": sc.label, "cycle": cycle, "cutoff": cutoff, "findings": out[:5]}


def cmd_shadow(a):
    t0 = time.monotonic()
    day = day_or_today(a.day)
    cycle = cycle_for_day(day, a.cycle)
    reg, sc, own_fence, _, _, lens_doc = resolve_scope_one(a.scope)
    if sc.profile_error:
        raise Refused("scope %s: %s" % (sc.label, sc.profile_error))
    now = dt.datetime.now().astimezone()
    ran, col_errors = run_collectors(sc, lens_doc, now, record_receipts=False)
    rec_c = reconcile_carried(sc, day, own_fence)
    rs = research_status(day, now)
    dl = deep_lens_for(reg, sc, lens_doc, day)
    base = read_baseline(sc)
    cells, extra = scope_cells(sc, lens_doc, own_fence, now)
    scope_state(sc, own_fence, base, None)
    m = manifest(sc, lens_doc, cells, extra, now, None, base)
    counts = {}
    for c in cells:
        counts[c["state"]] = counts.get(c["state"], 0) + 1
    m_dir = sc.anchor / "meetings" if sc.anchor and not own_fence(sc.anchor) else None
    meetings_res = _inspect_meetings_dir(m_dir, repo_root=sc.anchor)
    f_obj = _shadow_findings(sc, lens_doc, cells, rec_c, meetings_res, day, cycle, m["cutoff"])
    det = _deterministic_finding_checks(f_obj, sc, lens_doc)
    mod_issues, critic_meta = _run_blinded_critic(f_obj, sc, require_model=False)
    if det:
        raise Refused("shadow findings failed validation: " + "; ".join(det))
    out_root = Path(a.out).expanduser() if a.out else (state_dir() / "shadow" / sc.label.replace(":", "-") / day)
    (out_root / "evolve").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    f_path = out_root / "evolve" / ("%s.findings.json" % day)
    md_path = out_root / "evolve" / ("%s.md" % day)
    f_path.write_text(json.dumps(f_obj, indent=1) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    md_lines = [
        "# Evolve (shadow) — %s — %s (%s)" % (sc.label, day, cycle), "",
        "## Reconciled",
        "- Carried findings: %d (%d routed, %d due benefit checks)" % (rec_c["carried_total"], len(rec_c["routed"]), len(rec_c["due_checks"])), "",
        "## Deep lens: %s" % dl,
        "- Outside research: `%s`" % ("complete" if rs["outside"] == "complete" else "outside: stale"),
        "- Records target: `%s`" % ("vault" if sc.vault_records else "anchor-records-branch"), "",
        "## Findings (%d)" % len(f_obj["findings"]),
    ]
    for fd in f_obj["findings"]:
        md_lines.append("- **%s** (`%s`, `%s`, `%s`): %s — check: `%s`" % (
            fd["id"], fd["kind"], fd["lens"], fd["outcome_class"], fd["observation"], fd["acceptance_check"]))
    md_lines += ["", "## Feedback from the owner", ""]
    md_path.write_text("\n".join(md_lines), encoding="utf-8")
    wall = round(time.monotonic() - t0, 3)
    with_check = sum(1 for fd in f_obj["findings"] if (fd.get("acceptance_check") or "").strip())
    summary = {
        "scope": sc.label, "day": day, "cycle": cycle, "vault_records": sc.vault_records,
        "deep_lens": dl, "outside": rs["outside"], "collectors_ran": ran, "collector_errors": col_errors,
        "coverage_counts": counts, "reconciled": rec_c, "meetings": meetings_res["state"],
        "findings_count": len(f_obj["findings"]), "findings_with_check": with_check,
        "wall_seconds": wall, "split_needed": wall > 2400.0,
        "critic": {"issues": mod_issues, "meta": critic_meta},
        "out_dir": str(out_root) if not sc.confidential else None,
    }
    (out_root / "evolve" / ("%s-shadow.json" % day)).write_text(json.dumps(summary, indent=1) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps(summary, indent=1))
    else:
        print("shadow %s (%s): %d finding%s (%d with runnable check), deep-lens %s, outside %s, %.2fs (split_needed=%s)" % (
            sc.label, cycle, summary["findings_count"], "" if summary["findings_count"] == 1 else "s",
            with_check, dl, rs["outside"], wall, summary["split_needed"]))
    return 0


def main(argv=None):
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog=PROG, description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0])
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd")
    p = sub.add_parser("probes", help="the owner's answer surface, end to end, zero tokens")
    p.add_argument("--doc", action="append", default=[], help="also probe this real doc's links and render (read-only)")
    p.add_argument("--board", action="store_true", help="also probe the docs keel list finds with decisions open")
    p.add_argument("--limit", type=int, default=10)
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--no-record", action="store_true")
    p = sub.add_parser("coverage", help="the register of lens x source, the surface nothing reads, the quiet manifest")
    p.add_argument("--scope", help="one scope's cells and manifest (the surface is the deployment's: left out)")
    p.add_argument("--since", help="the last complete cutoff (ISO time); default: the last complete pass's manifest's")
    p.add_argument("--open", action="store_true", help="the pass's opening run: also writes the manifest --promote takes")
    p.add_argument("--promote", action="store_true",
                   help="the pass completed: its opening run's manifest becomes the scope's baseline (with --scope)")
    p.add_argument("--session", help="with --open or --promote: the pass's own session id, whose transcript is no change")
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--no-record", action="store_true")
    p = sub.add_parser("conformance", help="the rules against the transcripts: dead, holds, violated, worked around")
    p.add_argument("--scope")
    p.add_argument("--days", type=int, default=7)
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--no-record", action="store_true")
    p = sub.add_parser("validate", help="a record or a JSON-lines ledger against its schema")
    p.add_argument("kind")
    p.add_argument("file")
    p.add_argument("--scope", help="also accept outcome_classes declared in this scope's profile")
    p.add_argument("--quiet", action="store_true")
    p = sub.add_parser("schema", help="the schemas, or one as JSON")
    p.add_argument("kind", nargs="?")
    p = sub.add_parser("action-id", help="hash(finding id, action version, target scope)")
    p.add_argument("finding_id")
    p.add_argument("action_version", type=int)
    p.add_argument("target_scope")
    p = sub.add_parser("where", help="where a scope's pass reads and writes, and whether it is ready")
    p.add_argument("scope")
    p.add_argument("--day")
    p = sub.add_parser("open", help="zero-token collectors, carried reconcile, deep lens and opening manifest")
    p.add_argument("scope")
    p.add_argument("--day")
    p.add_argument("--cycle")
    p.add_argument("--session")
    p.add_argument("--quiet-exit", action="store_true", help="exit 3 and write a quiet receipt when quiet is earned")
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    p = sub.add_parser("critic", help="blinded cold-artefact critic over a findings JSON file")
    p.add_argument("file")
    p.add_argument("--scope")
    p.add_argument("--require-model", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    p = sub.add_parser("record", help="validate and land a scope pass's findings, receipt and baseline")
    p.add_argument("scope")
    p.add_argument("--day")
    p.add_argument("--cycle")
    p.add_argument("--session")
    p.add_argument("--cost", type=float)
    p.add_argument("--quiet", action="store_true")
    p = sub.add_parser("meetings", help="repo-committed meeting pre-briefs and dated if-then commitments")
    p.add_argument("path", nargs="?")
    p.add_argument("--scope")
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    p = sub.add_parser("replay", help="hidden-future replay at a cutoff with canary leak detection")
    p.add_argument("--cutoff", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--asks")
    p.add_argument("--findings")
    p.add_argument("--window", type=int, default=28)
    p.add_argument("--strict-cutoff", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    p = sub.add_parser("shadow", help="run a scope's pass in shadow without touching live refs or the vault")
    p.add_argument("--scope", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--day")
    p.add_argument("--cycle")
    p.add_argument("--out")
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)
    cmds = {"probes": cmd_probes, "coverage": cmd_coverage, "conformance": cmd_conformance, "validate": cmd_validate,
            "schema": cmd_schema, "action-id": cmd_action_id, "where": cmd_where, "open": cmd_open,
            "critic": cmd_critic, "record": cmd_record, "meetings": cmd_meetings, "replay": cmd_replay,
            "shadow": cmd_shadow}
    if a.cmd in cmds:
        try:
            return cmds[a.cmd](a)
        except Refused as e:
            print("%s %s: %s" % (PROG, a.cmd, e), file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        except Exception as e:   # noqa: BLE001  a crash is "could not tell", never 1 (blind spots: AGENTS.md)
            # the type alone: an OSError's text names its path, a confidential repo's included (the finish review)
            print("%s %s: could not finish (%s)" % (PROG, a.cmd, type(e).__name__), file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    ap.print_help(sys.stderr)
    return 2


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
